Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T02:25:44-07:00","id":1232070,"title":"","content":"The kickstarter goal is reached! Now wat's the next step?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T02:40:02-07:00","id":1232073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1232070#post1232070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The kickstarter goal is reached! Now wat's the next step?</div> </div> </div> </div>the two current stretch goals are shown upthread by Second chances, but there are goals at 65,000 and 75,000 to add &quot;mementos&quot;, and &quot;krewe regalia and ceremonies&quot; to the companion respectivly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T04:40:59-07:00","id":1232084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1232035#post1232035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rich talks about it more in today's MMN: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/2nd-chance-for-the-game-of-second-chancesmonday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/2nd-chance-fo...meeting-notes/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Can anyone summarise the diggerences between 1.0 and 1.1?<br /> Also, what led to the attitude shift at Onyx Path from &quot;lets update and rerelease one of our worst selling products&quot; to &quot;lets not waste money and time on erratas or FAQs on our bestselling products&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T04:51:55-07:00","id":1232085,"title":"","content":"What was Geist 1.1 if not a massive, funded errata?<br /> <br /> EDIT: okay, so that was a bit flip.<br /> <br /> Short version - doing the errata collection pass you will surely have seen happen on these forums before a pod version goes live is an enshrined responsibility of a dev, included in our fees. Back in the WW days, it wasn't - you printed the book before any fan ever saw it and could not do anything about it. I was rereading Seers of the Throne the other day and found a cringeworthy number of typos in it, including parts I wrote. It is roughly contemporary with Geist 1e.<br /> <br /> OPP does not have the resources to put contractor-devs like Danielle, myself, and Travis on retainer forever in order to pay us for FAQs, blogs, and continuing support. Some of us have day jobs that are okay with one-off book contracts but would actively prevent us from taking such a retainer anyway. WW didn't either - the handful of FAQs released either at OPP or WW have always been voluntary by the people involved.<br /> <br /> TLDR - OPP do spend money on errata where WW didn't. There's perfectly good reasons why a Dev hired for two years to make a game cannot commit to FAQing that game beyond that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 07-03-2018, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T04:56:56-07:00","id":1232087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1232042#post1232042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First Changeling and now Geist. All when I can\u2019t pay up for Reasons. Sigt. I\u2019m seething with jealousy here. <br /> <br /> Speaking of which, some questions that I hope don\u2019t compromise the rights of those who paid; can Bound/ghosts/Geists come from intense jealousy? Common in Asian ghost stories. And speaking of ghosts, what are the Absent absent of? What makes them different from regular ghosts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Smells like one of the Hungry to me (Bound who made the Bargain because they still had something they wanted), and from the looks of it anything that can tie you to reality can make you a ghost, so...<br /> <br /> We don't know the Absent yet, but from the Glossary they seem to be memory merchants who use their wares to escape from the Underworld. Wouldn't be surprised if they're called that because &quot;the world knows we're gone from it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T05:06:48-07:00","id":1232090,"title":"","content":"Plus the living remembering the Dead is one way ghosts get Essence. Buying and selling memories might be how Essence can be traded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T07:41:38-07:00","id":1232117,"title":"","content":"The relationship between Burden and Krewe Archetype is interesting, and I think that's supposed to be reflected in the two (or two of the three technically) described endgame scenarios. I do wonder whether a Bound can still have an Archetype without being a member of a Krewe. Perhaps that will be discussed in a later portion of the manuscript.<br /> <br /> (I'm also surprised that, what with the comparison to AA groups, the Heresy section for Necropolitans doesn't include the fact that the first step can be quite the doozy.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T13:38:33-07:00","id":1232217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1232042#post1232042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First Changeling and now Geist. All when I can\u2019t pay up for Reasons. Sigt. I\u2019m seething with jealousy here.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, some questions that I hope don\u2019t compromise the rights of those who paid; can Bound/ghosts/Geists come from intense jealousy? Common in Asian ghost stories. And speaking of ghosts, what are the Absent absent of? What makes them different from regular ghosts?</div> </div> </div> </div> The Absent are what they call playable ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T16:07:27-07:00","id":1232246,"title":"","con