lusion to that in the text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T10:49:40-07:00","id":1234329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1234328#post1234328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure there was a direct allusion to that in the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mon dieu, it seems you are right. That is what I get for reading something while still in the process of waking up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T11:19:53-07:00","id":1234336,"title":"","content":"The part about Dopplegangers intrigues me. Maybe a antagonist that can weaponize his dopplegangers? also I want ghost dogs.<br /> <br /> and on kickstarter news, we reached Ready made characters!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T11:29:22-07:00","id":1234338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1234329#post1234329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mon dieu, it seems you are right. That is what I get for reading something while still in the process of waking up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also worth noting (because I worked at a zoo) that aside from the meme, there are probably lots of Rank 1 Barghest floating around at zoos. Keepers get very attached to the animals in their care, especially the ones that have long lifespans. And in the cases where something goes horribly wrong and an animal has to be put down... odds are the person putting them down will fail their Breaking Point. Zookeepers see animals as individuals, not as creatures. Having to kill one of them is like having to kill your own family. And that's before you take the media into account.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T11:31:30-07:00","id":1234340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1234336#post1234336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The part about Dopplegangers intrigues me. Maybe a antagonist that can weaponize his dopplegangers? also I want ghost dogs.<br /> <br /> and on kickstarter news, we reached Ready made characters!</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like excellent fodder for a necromancer if you ask me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T11:41:20-07:00","id":1234342,"title":"","content":"I had a Mage antagonist in a chronicle who'd enslaved his own doppleganger as a Familiar","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T11:42:58-07:00","id":1234345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1234342#post1234342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a Mage antagonist in a chronicle who'd enslaved his own doppleganger as a Familiar</div> </div> </div> </div>Fucking mages,am I right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T11:44:41-07:00","id":1234346,"title":"","content":"Now I'm imagining a dentist somewhere in Minnesota being haunted by his much-publicized big-game trophies....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T11:45:26-07:00","id":1234347,"title":"","content":"There must be a Sin-Eater whose geist is a boat. Surely there's some way for an object to metaphysically trigger the 'drink' response at one of the rivers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T11:52:11-07:00","id":1234349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1234347#post1234347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There must be a Sin-Eater whose geist is a boat. Surely there's some way for an object to metaphysically trigger the 'drink' response at one of the rivers.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;...and this is my Geist, Boaty McBoatface.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>(Foghorn noises in the distance)</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T11:53:26-07:00","id":1234350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1234338#post1234338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also worth noting (because I worked at a zoo) that aside from the meme, there are probably lots of Rank 1 Barghest floating around at zoos. Keepers get very attached to the animals in their care, especially the ones that have long lifespans. And in the cases where something goes horribly wrong and an animal has to be put down... odds are the person putting them down will fail their Breaking Point. Zookeepers see animals as individuals, not as creatures. Having to kill one of them is like having to kill your own family. And that's before you take the media into account.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats why I am torn on having ectophagia on Barghest not be a breaking point. The ghostly eating of a beloved pet or zoo animal feels like it should hurt your integrity(or I guess synergy in this case) somehow because in the end you are just doing it for power and not survival. I myself would most likely homebrew that it would be a breaking point but maybe not a crisis point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T12:14:54-07:00","id":1234357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1234349#post1234349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;...and this is my Geist, Boaty McBoatface.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>(Foghorn noises in the distance)</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I can't be the only one who read this and immediately thought of the Flying Dutchman as a Geist.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T12:23:30-07:00","id":1234359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1234350#post1234350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thats why I am torn on having ectophagia on Barghest not be a breaking point. The ghostly eating of a beloved pet or zoo animal feels like it should hurt your integrity(or I guess synergy in this case) somehow because in the end you are just doing it for power and not survival. I myself would most likely homebrew that it would be a breaking point but maybe not a crisis point.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that from how I understand the new Synergy system, the one to suffer from &quot;breaking points&quot; is the geist, not the Bound. The Sin Eater have no psychological mechanism which cares about emotional trauma and to separate &quot;right&quot; from &quot;wrong&quot;. That's the geist's job- and we are talking about a minor death god which barely remembers it was once human. Geists care about Ectophagia, not the Bound, and if they are fine with eating the ghosts of animals, than while the Sin Eater may be disgusted by the thought, it would cause no mental trauma to them. The benefits of being dead, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T12:24:43-07:00","id":1234360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1234342#post1234342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a Mage antagonist in a chronicle who'd enslaved his own doppleganger as a Familiar</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How can you enslave a familiar? I though the familiar bond was voluntary, and can be broken by either party at any time. <br /> <br /> Under current rules, enslaving a ghost is certainly possible, even easy for some mages and others, but as a familiar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T12:58:13-07:00","id":1234368,"title":"","content":"Seems like at that point while it may be voluntary, a mage can control what a ghost or spirit volunteers to do in the first place. It's probably a better way to deal with Rank 2s, especially since their own desires can be troublesomely independent. Basically two separate acts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1234357#post1234357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't be the only one who read this and immediately thought of the Flying Dutchman as a Geist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking Knightboat, then Roger Corman's Titanic, for some reasons the Simpsons are on my mind. But the idea's the same. Maybe a river of gasoline for a modern boat, or some steamy one that has gusts of wind, or a tarry river where the tar sinks into the ephemeral material of the boat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-12-2018, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T14:23:05-07:00","id":1234401,"title":"","content":"One of the ideas I\u2019ve been kicking around since first edition is \u201cthe living haunted house\u201d (an antagonist who has a haunted mansion as his geist, with all the accompanying ghosts of residents piled in). I\u2019m certain that I can play with castoffs enough to make that work at some point. I\u2019m quite excited for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T14:46:51-07:00","id":1234410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1234338#post1234338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also worth noting (because I worked at a zoo) that aside from the meme, there are probably lots of Rank 1 Barghest floating around at zoos. Keepers get very attached to the animals in their care, especially the ones that have long lifespans. And in the cases where something goes horribly wrong and an animal has to be put down... odds are the person putting them down will fail their Breaking Point. Zookeepers see animals as individuals, not as creatures. Having to kill one of them is like having to kill your own family. And that's before you take the media into account.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair and also heartbreaking point. I might have to reread Sy Montgomery's <i>The Soul of an Octopus</i> if I ever end up running a game of Geist.<br /> <br /> EDIT: A weird thought that suddenly zoomed into my mind: What if the reason that the Bound don't have a full Integrity-analog is because they don't have an actual soul anymore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 07-12-2018, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T15:17:43-07:00","id":1234420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1234410#post1234410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A weird thought that suddenly zoomed into my mind: What if the reason that the Bound don't have a full Integrity-analog is because they don't have an actual soul anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, ghosts do have Integrity- but that's more or less also what I think. The Bound are walking, talking, nice looking corpse, ridden by a shade which has forsaken every semblance of humanity in order to escape its prison. The geist <i>is</i> their soul, or at least its equivalent- it sits in the same place, after all, so it makes sense that they fill the same role. That's why Synergy is such a big thing for Sin Eaters- it measures how well their soul-replacement is connected to their body, and putting their geist to the edge harms that connection. <br /> <br /> When you think about it, it is also means something really powerful about the Sin Eater existence- there is no mechanic or force which punish them for their sins, and no god which bless them for their virtues. Yes, that means that the Bound can kill innocent people if they want, if not worse- it is just that most of them don't want to. When a Bound shows mercy toward the living or compassion toward the dead, it is not because they are compelled to by an alien mindset enforce upon them by the conditions of their existence. They are not trapped in a spiral downward, nor do they need to balance between two worlds or are forced into constant progress. When the Bound so something good, it is because they chose to do so, because they wanted to do so. The same for doing something bad. The Sin Eaters are the ones to decide their own path, to chose their own actions, to do whatever they wish in order to gain their second chance in life. The Sin Eaters are <i>free</i>, and when they relieve themselves from their Burden, they did so in the way they chose, walking the path they decided and lived their second life to its very end. If they fail again, it all their fault- but if they succeed, the success is all their own, be it be solving their own personal pain, changing the very nature of the world or by becoming gods of death by their own right. The win is all their own, for better and worse.<br /> <br /> I find it pretty awesome, if you'll ask me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T15:35:26-07:00","id":1234422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1234420#post1234420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When you think about it, it is also means something really powerful about the Sin Eater existence- there is no mechanic or force which punish them for their sins, and no god which bless them for their virtues. Yes, that means that the Bound can kill innocent people if they want, if not worse- it is just that most of them don't want to. When a Bound shows mercy toward the living or compassion toward the dead, it is not because they are compelled to by an alien mindset enforce upon them by the conditions of their existence. They are not trapped in a spiral downward, nor do they need to balance between two worlds or are forced into constant progress. When the Bound so something good, it is because they chose to do so, because they wanted to do so. The same for doing something bad. The Sin Eaters are the ones to decide their own path, to chose their own actions, to do whatever they wish in order to gain their second chance in life. The Sin Eaters are <i>free</i>, and when they relieve themselves from their Burden, they did so in the way they chose, walking the path they decided and lived their second life to its very end. If they fail again, it all their fault- but if they succeed, the success is all their own, be it be solving their own personal pain, changing the very nature of the world or by becoming gods of death by their own right. The win is all their own, for better and worse.<br /> <br /> I find it pretty awesome, if you'll ask me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Replace \u201cthe Bound\u201d and \u201csin-eater\u201d with \u201cBeast\u201d or \u201cthe Begotten,\u201d change a few things to fit context and that\u2019s how I view the two games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T17:44:55-07:00","id":1234462,"title":"","content":"Now, I'm afraid I don't have the most experience with the Chronicles in-play, and I'm having a titch of trouble wrapping my head around this particular aspect from the corebook, so if I may ask: How horrific is a Rank 5 ghost, and how awesome would it be to Unleash it at every opportunity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2444-lindhrive","name":"Lindhrive","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T18:04:34-07:00","id":1234468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lindhrive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1234462#post1234462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I'm afraid I don't have the most experience with the Chronicles in-play, and I'm having a titch of trouble wrapping my head around this particular aspect from the corebook, so if I may ask: How horrific is a Rank 5 ghost, and how awesome would it be to Unleash it at every opportunity?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Rank 5 geist, when Unleashed, has five dots of Influence in its innate Key along with access to the Haunts of its Sin-Eater, which it uses with Power + Rank + Haunt. It's also a Materialized ephemeral being (with all that implies) and it uses Down and Dirty Combat against lesser ghosts and untemplated mortals.<br /> <br /> The tradeoff, as ever, is that if you aren't getting there by steering crisis points through high Synergy, then you're spending the scene unable to heal \u2014 and if you wind up in a circumstance where your geist's bane is in play, there's a good chance that's going to stick for an extra scene after you've spent your one freebie for the chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T18:16:10-07:00","id":1234477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1234468#post1234468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Rank 5 geist, when Unleashed, has five dots of Influence in its innate Key along with access to the Haunts of its Sin-Eater, which it uses with Power + Rank + Haunt. It's also a Materialized ephemeral being (with all that implies) and it uses Down and Dirty Combat against lesser ghosts and untemplated mortals.<br /> <br /> The tradeoff, as ever, is that if you aren't getting there by steering crisis points through high Synergy, then you're spending the scene unable to heal \u2014 and if you wind up in a circumstance where your geist's bane is in play, there's a good chance that's going to stick for an extra scene after you've spent your one freebie for the chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Keys are very abstract, so I'm not sure what you can really do with them in practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T18:19:20-07:00","id":1234479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1234422#post1234422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Replace \u201cthe Bound\u201d and \u201csin-eater\u201d with \u201cBeast\u201d or \u201cthe Begotten,\u201d change a few things to fit context and that\u2019s how I view the two games.</div> </div> </div> </div> Beasts are largely rewarded for tormenting people, their integrity stat is wired backwards to say a morals or vampires, it's pushes them towards immortality rather then away from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T18:28:08-07:00","id":1234483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1234477#post1234477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Keys are very abstract, so I'm not sure what you can really do with them in practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Keys are disease/poison, bad luck/complex danger, animals, blood/passion, silence/shadow, and the four classical elements. These are not Influences that present a greater challenge to apply than others do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T19:21:33-07:00","id":1234491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1234479#post1234479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beasts are largely rewarded for tormenting people, their integrity stat is wired backwards to say a morals or vampires, it's pushes them towards immortality rather then away from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. That\u2019s the point. There\u2019s no negative incentives for being immoral, instead there being positive incentives for being monstrous, which would largely lead to immorality. So being moral in spite of all this means even more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T19:55:20-07:00","id":1234499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1234327#post1234327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So an animal whose death causes or at least risks Integrity loss in a human has a level of power and awareness as a ghost.<br /> <br /> Which means that there is a greater than zero-percent chance that there is a Sin-Eater in the world bound to the Geist of Harambe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget Grape-kun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T20:49:00-07:00","id":1234516,"title":"","content":"Re: Ectophagia on Barghests. Yes, those animals became ghosts because someone cared enough about them that their death was a Breaking Point. But unless somehow it was the specific Sin-Eater whose care created the Barghest, I can see ectophagia not being a breaking point. No, I don't wanna eat the ghost of <i>my </i>cat, no matter how dire the situation -- but eating any random ghost-cat I came across, especially if I'm hard up for Plasm, is not the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T02:37:54-07:00","id":1234566,"title":"","content":"Are there going to be more Archetypes in the final book, or are we only getting the five? i'm already coming up with ideas for NPCs, but not all of them fit the current archetypes. For example, I have an NPC that fits the Vengeful Burden quiet nicely, but she would be more about punishing criminals, not bringing them to justice. Or another character that uses ghosts like a resource (using ghosts to form a giant surveillance web spanning the city so he can spy on everyone). Are heresies supposed to cover these kinds of characters? Is the first one I mentioned just a Fury heretic? Or are geists who don't fit into the archetypes just not given one, so the first NPC would just be Vengeful with no Archetype at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T03:07:08-07:00","id":1234569,"title":"","content":"I assume there are going to be more Archetypes if we are following the lexicon section, but it seems they would be more of antagonist material than protagonist","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T03:29:25-07:00","id":1234571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1234566#post1234566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there going to be more Archetypes in the final book, or are we only getting the five? i'm already coming up with ideas for NPCs, but not all of them fit the current archetypes. For example, I have an NPC that fits the Vengeful Burden quiet nicely, but she would be more about punishing criminals, not bringing them to justice. Or another character that uses ghosts like a resource (using ghosts to form a giant surveillance web spanning the city so he can spy on everyone). Are heresies supposed to cover these kinds of characters? Is the first one I mentioned just a Fury heretic? Or are geists who don't fit into the archetypes just not given one, so the first NPC would just be Vengeful with no Archetype at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I understand, Furies can be judges jury and executioners, as long as it fit their idea of Justice. How else could they deal with murderous ghosts and other supernaturals ?<br /> Using ghost for your own gain is Bonepicker, an antagonist Archetype. But nothing prevent other Krewes to use ghosts to follow their Archetype: the ghost spy network is cited as exemple in the Furies entry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T03:40:14-07:00","id":1234572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1234569#post1234569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume there are going to be more Archetypes if we are following the lexicon section, but it seems they would be more of antagonist material than protagonist</div> </div> </div> </div>In this particular case I was thinking about them as NPCs, yes (the first as a villain, the second as a neutral source of information), but I know plenty of players that could easily make either into a character. The first is basically The Crow (or Ghost Rider, or Punisher). The second could be something like a vodoun geist that makes bargains with ghosts, again seeing ghosts as a resource rather than as things to be avenged/studied/entertained/saved/etc. Both legitimate character concepts that can't really be done with the current Archetypes (unless &quot;no Archetype&quot; is a valid option).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T03:50:59-07:00","id":1234577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Doppelg\u00e4nger who fully consumes another ghost of the same person gains 1 Rank. </div> </div> </div>Does this mean all ghosts are able to commit ectophagia or just Doppelg\u00e4nger? Only Bound are mentioned to be able to commit ectophagia in the manuscript. I also realise that the rules for ectophagia doesn't specify either dice pool (if there is one) or how long it takes. 1 Plasm per turn? All Plasm immediately? Up to their Plasm per turn limit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T03:54:40-07:00","id":1234579,"title":"","content":"You haven't had the ghost rules yet - they're in next week's chunk of the text. Patience, padawan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 07-13-2018, 07:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T05:10:39-07:00","id":1234596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1234516#post1234516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Ectophagia on Barghests. Yes, those animals became ghosts because someone cared enough about them that their death was a Breaking Point. But unless somehow it was the specific Sin-Eater whose care created the Barghest, I can see ectophagia not being a breaking point. No, I don't wanna eat the ghost of <i>my </i>cat, no matter how dire the situation -- but eating any random ghost-cat I came across, especially if I'm hard up for Plasm, is not the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get it, thats why I said I would house rule it with my group. other people might feel differently but I feel like eating something that was alive that meant so much to a person or people that I feel like a geist would react to that somehow. maybe thats just me, I don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T07:59:53-07:00","id":1234641,"title":"","content":"So there\u2019s grape-kun BarghestI in Japan","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T09:23:10-07:00","id":1234669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1234401#post1234401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the ideas I\u2019ve been kicking around since first edition is \u201cthe living haunted house\u201d (an antagonist who has a haunted mansion as his geist, with all the accompanying ghosts of residents piled in). I\u2019m certain that I can play with castoffs enough to make that work at some point. I\u2019m quite excited for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there is a roll involved on Ghost-on-Ghost Ectophagia, and the Dramatic Failure involves the &quot;victim&quot; instead taking a bite out of the aggressor, then it <i>could</i> be possible for a Ghost to try and eat a Castoff house and fail so badly at it that the house eats them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T09:27:28-07:00","id":1234671,"title":"","content":"So, the Phantom Limb merit lets you use your doppelganger missing parts. Baring the obvious immediate ramifications of their loss, would it be possible to have things like Phantom Hearts, Stomachs, or even Brains?<br /> <br /> And why not Phantom Teeth? Some people are very attached to theirs. [/joking]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T16:53:30-07:00","id":1234822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1234671#post1234671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And why not Phantom Teeth? Some people are very attached to theirs. [/joking]</div> </div> </div> </div> would phantom teeth let you. It\u2019s through a ghost? Would they let you eat a ghost? Oh gosh. The eaters of the deal could be really literal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24316-mrowl","name":"MrOwl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T17:03:42-07:00","id":1234824,"title":"","content":"I imagine it would be more like chattering teeth than phantasmal devourers of things. Maybe the Tooth Fairy from Manhunter and Red Dragon would leave behind ghost dentures that would haunt people and bite them in the night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T14:16:05-07:00","id":1235082,"title":"","content":"In today's update, Travis goes into the differences between 1e and 2e Geist (and references how out of all the past CofD 2e updates, Geist is the one that's received the most drastic changes) and goes into why the changes in between editions were made. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/geist-the-sin-eaters-2nd-edition/posts/2238332\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/2238332</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T18:06:48-07:00","id":1235122,"title":"","content":"Man these previews are so good. The question of &quot;ok but what do you do&quot; has been answered thoroughly. I'm a little bummed about certain manifestation variants that didn't survive the transition, but the new Haunts are way more thematically coherent and easy to remember. <br /> <br /> I saw this question asked but not answered previously: Is there intended to be something preventing a Sin Eater from unlocking a Haunt with a Key and using one of the bonus plasm points to ward off the Doom? I like the Dooms, they do a great job of balancing carrot and stick in a way that CoD games often struggle with, but even if you can turn them to an advantage it seems like it would be faster to just repeatedly use Keys -1 bonus Plasm until you had a full pool and that feels... off","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T18:44:03-07:00","id":1235132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1235122#post1235122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it seems like it would be faster to just repeatedly use Keys -1 bonus Plasm until you had a full pool and that feels... off</div> </div> </div> </div>Using a Key without getting the Doomed Condition requires that you:<br /> 1. Be using it with a Haunt, a power which itself costs at least 1 Plasm and does not end until its baseline Condition does (which is easier/less prone to complication with some Haunts than others but still mostly requires you to have a target), and<br /> 2. Spend an additional 1 Plasm on the Haunt, thus requiring that you use a Key whose Unlock Attribute is 3 or higher in order to receive a net gain in your Plasm total.<br /> <br /> For contrast, you can instead use that Key in a resonant situation for heightened odds of exceptional success, which gives you back half the Plasm you spent on the Haunt after it ends without difficulty in addition to exempting you from the Doom.<br /> <br /> So, in short, you can't get the free Plasm without the Doom unless you use a Haunt and you stand to get better returns from just using the Key normally \u2014 and in cases like &quot;what if I Extrude the Caul over and over,&quot; you have the fact that annoying your geist can give you a Condition that makes dealing with it harder to manage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T18:46:14-07:00","id":1235388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1235132#post1235132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using a Key without getting the Doomed Condition requires that you:<br /> 1. Be using it with a Haunt, a power which itself costs at least 1 Plasm and does not end until its baseline Condition does (which is easier/less prone to complication with some Haunts than others but still mostly requires you to have a target), and<br /> 2. Spend an additional 1 Plasm on the Haunt, thus requiring that you use a Key whose Unlock Attribute is 3 or higher in order to receive a net gain in your Plasm total.<br /> <br /> For contrast, you can instead use that Key in a resonant situation for heightened odds of exceptional success, which gives you back half the Plasm you spent on the Haunt after it ends without difficulty in addition to exempting you from the Doom.<br /> <br /> So, in short, you can't get the free Plasm without the Doom unless you use a Haunt and you stand to get better returns from just using the Key normally \u2014 and in cases like &quot;what if I Extrude the Caul over and over,&quot; you have the fact that annoying your geist can give you a Condition that makes dealing with it harder to manage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even without spending 1 Plasm to negate the Doom, any Sin-Eater with the Stillness Key can just use any Haunt (Curse, for example) accept the Doom, then speak to Resolve it. Rinse, repeat. Heck, RAW, with Curse it turns into a Beat-Machine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Curse</b><br /> ...<br /> <b>Resolution:</b><br /> \u2022 Another Sin-Eater counters the Curse (p. XX).<br /> \u2022 The Curse mark comes into contact with the Ban or Bane of the creating Sin-Eater\u2019s geist.<br /> \u2022 <u>When this Condition resolves, the Sin-Eater who created it also takes a Beat.</u> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Key of Stillness</b><br /> ...<br /> <b>Doom:</b> The next time your character speaks even a single word, <u>resolve this Doom and the Condition from the Haunt she unlocked with the Key of Stillness</u>. </div> </div> </div>Looks to me like:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Activate Stillness Curse on random target. Reap Composure - 1 Plasm. Accept Doom.</li> <li>Speak.</li> <li>Stillness Doom and Curse Resolves. Gain a Beat.</li> <li>Being Doom-free and up Composure - 1 Plasm, repeat from step 1.</li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-15-2018, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T20:35:22-07:00","id":1235409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1235388#post1235388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, RAW, with Curse it turns into a Beat-Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>See again: &quot;annoying your geist by e.g. frivolously using its powers for stupid bullshit is a good way to get tapped out on Willpower very fast.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also take a look at the section on Beats and notice the clear statement about how that particular character advancement mechanic works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T20:36:49-07:00","id":1235411,"title":"","content":"New Stretch goal has a haunt section.I wonder what additional Haunts would be added to join the current list. The return of the Pit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T00:25:23-07:00","id":1235471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1235411#post1235411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Stretch goal has a haunt section.I wonder what additional Haunts would be added to join the current list. The return of the Pit?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure if it would be new Haunts, or expansion on how to use Haunts and how they mix with Keys.<br /> <br /> Also add me in the &quot;The cost of 1 Plasm to avoid doom makes it too easy to use Keys&quot; camp. Sure you might still lose Plasm overall but you also get 2-3 extra dice to activate your powers, so it still feels like a net free bonus to me compared to using a &quot;vanilla&quot; Haunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T03:40:05-07:00","id":1235497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1235409#post1235409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See again: &amp;quot;annoying your geist by e.g. frivolously using its powers for stupid bullshit is a good way to get tapped out on Willpower very fast.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Also take a look at the section on Beats and notice the clear statement about how that particular character advancement mechanic works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you cite where these <u>rules</u> are listed? I don't recall seeing them in the manuscript so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T03:47:18-07:00","id":1235499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1235471#post1235471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm not sure if it would be new Haunts, or expansion on how to use Haunts and how they mix with Keys.<br /> <br /> Also add me in the &amp;quot;The cost of 1 Plasm to avoid doom makes it too easy to use Keys&amp;quot; camp. Sure you might still lose Plasm overall but you also get 2-3 extra dice to activate your powers, so it still feels like a net free bonus to me compared to using a &amp;quot;vanilla&amp;quot; Haunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>A better alternative might be a scaling cost such as it costing 1 additional Plasm each time you use it to forestall a/that Key's Doom in a Scene (or Chapter). That way there are diminishing returns.<br /> <br /> Another alternative, would be to instead cost a point of Willpower (similar to a Demon suppressing Compromise when using an Exploit). Since you don't get the same resource from activation, it doesn't semi-automatically pay for itself. Willpower recovery tends to be a bit harder to game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T05:20:56-07:00","id":1235511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1235471#post1235471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm not sure if it would be new Haunts, or expansion on how to use Haunts and how they mix with Keys.<br /> <br /> Also add me in the &quot;The cost of 1 Plasm to avoid doom makes it too easy to use Keys&quot; camp. Sure you might still lose Plasm overall but you also get 2-3 extra dice to activate your powers, so it still feels like a net free bonus to me compared to using a &quot;vanilla&quot; Haunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting enough it might be both new haunts and an expansion on the ones already in the book depending on how it gets outlined in Memento Mori, according to James.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T05:27:48-07:00","id":1235513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1235497#post1235497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you cite where these <u>rules</u> are listed? I don't recall seeing them in the manuscript so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>PDF page 10 on second manuscript. You could probably just search for the first mention of Beats, too, its like three lines under that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T05:35:34-07:00","id":1235516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1235513#post1235513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> PDF page 10 on second manuscript. You could probably just search for the first mention of Beats, too, its like three lines under that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I reread that section. Nothing in there prohibits what I listed above, which is why I'm confused. The above can be utilized every scene to get 1 Beat from a Condition Resolving without any apparent repercussions (or multiple times during a Scene for the extra Plasm).<br /> <br /> And I still having seen anything about repeated Haunt use universally antagonizing a Geist and incurring a Willpower cost.<br /> <br /> NOTE: I'm referencing rules here, not intent (which can vary). Saying &quot;I don't consider that action Beat-worthy&quot; is an individual ST determination I'm not addressing here (as stated in my restricting to Rules-As-Written).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T05:41:10-07:00","id":1235518,"title":"","content":"Fingers crossed for the Stygian Key and the Pit making a comeback.<br /> <br /> re the &quot;Refueling plasm exploit&quot;, as ST I would put serious repercussions on such a thing: For one, they are repeatedly opening a door into the Underworld, and two, the Doomed condition is something like getting the Underworld's attention. The fluff literally says they find themselves controlled by the Old Laws that created the key. I imagine that doing this repeatedly, within a short time frame to boot, is not going to not have consequences. This is more than enough of an excuse for me as ST to <i>allow </i>this behaviour, but abuse the heck out of it to throw out repercussions to hell and back. Imagine the player's realization that the 'exploit' comes back to bite him in the ass severely when e.g. the Doom somehow gets 'stuck' (cannot be resolved for a few scenes) or he cannot stop oozing plasm, attracting more and more ghosts and with them, Reapers. Or have the Key 'break' under the stress of being used so often, and he has to do x to fix it. X could be something like going a night/day/week without spending Plasm, helping a certain number of ghosts pass on (preferably thematically appropriate to the Key), OR eat a certain ghost / sacrifice a ghost to the Key.<br /> You could also just have the Geist be pissed at having to do this stupid act over and over again. Especially Shroud and Coil could end with the Geist going &quot;nope, imma stay in control now, you've pushed me around enough'.<br /> All for a good story and good time at the table, of course.<br /> <br /> Regarding the Key of Stillness, I am more than certain that there will be an addition, since breaking the doom by just talking and no other drawback is too easily done. I can imagine that the Mute condition will instead be forced upon the player, or alternatively Deafened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T05:42:03-07:00","id":1235519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1235516#post1235516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I still having seen anything about repeated Haunt use universally antagonizing a Geist and incurring a Willpower cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possible Sources under the Wavering Condition, a thing which at its least-broadly-applied makes rolling <i>any dice pool that includes Synergy, e.g. every single Haunt, </i>require you to spend a point of Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T05:43:29-07:00","id":1235520,"title":"","content":"3Rd preview has just dropped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T06:00:03-07:00","id":1235525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1235519#post1235519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possible Sources under the Wavering Condition, a thing which at its least-broadly-applied makes rolling <i>any dice pool that includes Synergy, e.g. every single Haunt, </i>require you to spend a point of Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which <i>is subjective</i>. Nothing in the rules state that spamming Stillness Curse to keep topped up on Plasm would annoy your Geist, yes? Some might even appreciate the forethought.<br /> <br /> So, again, is there anything in the <u>rules</u> that prevents such? Or is it merely at the whims/discretion of the ST (which could cover any number of mechanics or situations)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T06:06:56-07:00","id":1235526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1235518#post1235518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">re the &quot;Refueling plasm exploit&quot;, as ST I would put serious repercussions on such a thing: For one, they are repeatedly opening a door into the Underworld, and two, the Doomed condition is something like getting the Underworld's attention. The fluff literally says they find themselves controlled by the Old Laws that created the key. I imagine that doing this repeatedly, within a short time frame to boot, is not going to not have consequences. This is more than enough of an excuse for me as ST to <i>allow </i>this behaviour, but abuse the heck out of it to throw out repercussions to hell and back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, definitely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1235518#post1235518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Key of Stillness, I am more than certain that there will be an addition, since breaking the doom by just talking and no other drawback is too easily done. I can imagine that the Mute condition will instead be forced upon the player, or alternatively Deafened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, having it remove without Resolving the associated Condition would be good. Having it transform into Mute Condition if the prior Haunt Condition Resolves/removes is a good idea too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T08:16:18-07:00","id":1235565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1235516#post1235516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I reread that section. Nothing in there prohibits what I listed above, which is why I'm confused. The above can be utilized every scene to get 1 Beat from a Condition Resolving without any apparent repercussions (or multiple times during a Scene for the extra Plasm).<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>You seemed to have missed this part on page 10: &quot;Scene Limit: You may only earn one Beat per category per scene.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T08:23:11-07:00","id":1235567,"title":"","content":"Can we talk about the preview now? <br /> <br /> I really like how Chthonians are often eldritch Underworld fish. They live (?) in the Rivers, of course they look somewhat aquatic. And ghosts will eat them if they can, because they are fish. <br /> <br /> Also, we got ourselves a Dominion Conquest system, for when you get sick of an Old Law. Or a Kerberos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T08:58:31-07:00","id":1235579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1235565#post1235565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You seemed to have missed this part on page 10: &quot;Scene Limit: You may only earn one Beat per category per scene.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not - &quot;<i>The above can be utilized <b>every scene</b> to get <b>1 Beat</b> from a Condition Resolving without any apparent repercussions</i>&quot; meaning you can use this for your once-per-scene instance of Condition Resolution. The bit in parentheses was that you can also use it more often to get more Plasm, though not Beats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T09:09:46-07:00","id":1235580,"title":"","content":"So, the &quot;Y-Splat&quot; of Krewe has its own &quot;Power Stat&quot; in the form of Esotery. If this is the prototype for organization rules, I wonder what form it will take for other Orgs.<br /> <br /> I'm loving the rest of the Organization rules so far (and not just because it parallels how I've thought about handling Organization-level entities).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-16-2018, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T09:18:55-07:00","id":1235581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1235579#post1235579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did not - &quot;<i>The above can be utilized <b>every scene</b> to get <b>1 Beat</b> from a Condition Resolving without any apparent repercussions</i>&quot; meaning you can use this for your once-per-scene instance of Condition Resolution. The bit in parentheses was that you can also use it more often to get more Plasm, though not Beats.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's not really a Beat-machine then, as you previouly asserted. A Plasm machine maybe, but not a Beat machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T09:20:07-07:00","id":1235582,"title":"","content":"So I have some questions on the Oracle haunt that are bothering me. <br /> <br /> The effects of the haunt are straightforward and I like them (being a good port from the 1stEd equivalent). So I understand the effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The part that I'm getting hooked up on is the in-universe justification for the haunt, i.e. what is happening to get those effects. The Manuscript says that you die and release your ghost from your body. The People (other than you) then ask your corpse questions according to what is allowed in that dot of the Oracle. How does your ghost find these things out? I mean at least the 5th dot said that your ghost has a weird fever dream of the future (essentially) as it walks through the underworld. But all other dots it just says your ghost knows these things. How? Other ghosts don't seem to randomly know things about other ghosts other than them. I just don't understand how this power is working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T09:35:03-07:00","id":1235587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1235580#post1235580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the &amp;quot;Y-Splat&amp;quot; of Krewe has its own &amp;quot;Power Stat&amp;quot; in the form of Esotery. If this is the prototype for organization rules, I wonder what form it will take for other Orgs.<br /> <br /> I'm loving the rest of the Organization rules so far (and not just because it parallels how I've thought about handling Organization-level entities).</div> </div> </div> </div>Deviant uses the base org system for antagonists - some of the traits are different, and there's more focus on &quot;downtime&quot; actions. Between the two games you should be able to do pretty much anything with a modicum of homebrew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T09:58:24-07:00","id":1235603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1235582#post1235582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I have some questions on the Oracle haunt that are bothering me.<br /> <br /> The effects of the haunt are straightforward and I like them (being a good port from the 1stEd equivalent). So I understand the effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The part that I'm getting hooked up on is the in-universe justification for the haunt, i.e. what is happening to get those effects. The Manuscript says that you die and release your ghost from your body. The People (other than you) then ask your corpse questions according to what is allowed in that dot of the Oracle. How does your ghost find these things out? I mean at least the 5th dot said that your ghost has a weird fever dream of the future (essentially) as it walks through the underworld. But all other dots it just says your ghost knows these things. How? Other ghosts don't seem to randomly know things about other ghosts other than them. I just don't understand how this power is working.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nobody knows where the coins that all ghosts come into existence with that allow them to open an Avernian Gate without being sucked through once come from either. It's a mystery and a plot hook to examine; to be frank, a Bound channeling that Haunt is effectively dying without actually being dead enough to send their geist into survive-at-all-costs mode; at that point, what is considered &quot;normal&quot; has gone out the window, and we aren't dealing with a normal ghost anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T10:05:48-07:00","id":1235605,"title":"","content":"Hey i was wondering something about krewe tasks/actions..like i know one should put logical limits on them like &quot;get us nominated for president&quot; when just being a small krewe with no political influence, but i did wonder what the mystical limits of such tasks? Like could a krewe decide that they want to try and make a life form or invent/find a ceremony to do((to use a vtr example of a similar effect you got the birthing the god ritual for cruac)) with a series of tasks or would that also not be feasible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T10:28:57-07:00","id":1235621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1235567#post1235567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we talk about the preview now? <br /> <br /> I really like how Chthonians are often eldritch Underworld fish. They live (?) in the Rivers, of course they look somewhat aquatic. And ghosts will eat them if they can, because they are fish. <br /> <br /> Also, we got ourselves a Dominion Conquest system, for when you get sick of an Old Law. Or a Kerberos.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Chthonians make me think of Chthulhu and similar Lovecraftian deities somehow. And Neon Genesis Evangelion's angels.<br /> Also, the Elder from Legacy Of Kain. Just less interested in people. <br /> I like them a lot, and thus am likely to Feature them quite a bit in my game.<br /> I like how Chthonian Fish are a source of Terror and food, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T10:58:31-07:00","id":1235636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1235621#post1235621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like how Chthonian Fish are a source of Terror and food, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, of course - they are high in <i><u>Omega</u></i>-3, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T11:35:09-07:00","id":1235652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1235636#post1235636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, of course - they are high in <i><u>Omega</u></i>-3, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>This made me groan. Well done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","cus