r - form a Krewe that acts as a Barghest sanctuary. Rehabilitate <i>all</i> the Barghests! Transform the Underworld into a giant petting zoo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T17:14:40-07:00","id":1236212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236206#post1236206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dream bigger - form a Krewe that acts as a Barghest sanctuary. Rehabilitate <i>all</i> the Barghests! Transform the Underworld into a giant petting zoo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, as that goes, I won't personally settle for anything less than the absolute destiny apocalypse-nothing less than the absolute shattering of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Buuuuut baby steps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T18:01:23-07:00","id":1236226,"title":"","content":"Goal after next adds The Wolf &amp; the Raven, and The Forbidding Lands to the 1e bundle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T18:18:09-07:00","id":1236233,"title":"","content":"Is it just me or is there some real resemblance between the Ocean of Fragments and the Ocean Ouroboros/Abyss we see here? As well as the Hermit and the Old Man? It really feels like the Ocean of Fragments is the Underworlds 'reflection' of the Abyss, but that might just be Mage Supremacy<span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2122.<br /> <br /> Also, I feel like the woman depicted on the lead coins all ghosts get is someone important in the big picture of the cosmology, anyone more into this that has some insight?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T18:34:29-07:00","id":1236243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236233#post1236233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me or is there some real resemblance between the Ocean of Fragments and the Ocean Ouroboros/Abyss we see here? As well as the Hermit and the Old Man? It really feels like the Ocean of Fragments is the Underworlds 'reflection' of the Abyss, but that might just be Mage Supremacy<span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2122.<br /> </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><br /> <br /> In a Geist-centric game, it could be the other way around - the ultimate bane of mages turning out to be the Underworld. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I feel like the woman depicted on the lead coins all ghosts get is someone important in the big picture of the cosmology, anyone more into this that has some insight? </div> </div> </div></span></span>I hear Wraith in the WoD has someone called the Lady of Fate; a nod to that figure, perhapa?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T18:36:27-07:00","id":1236244,"title":"","content":"She's probably a <i>lead</i>er of some sort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-17-2018, 11:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T18:38:26-07:00","id":1236246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236233#post1236233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me or is there some real resemblance between the Ocean of Fragments and the Ocean Ouroboros/Abyss we see here? As well as the Hermit and the Old Man? It really feels like the Ocean of Fragments is the Underworlds 'reflection' of the Abyss, but that might just be Mage Supremacy<span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2122.<br /> <br /> Also, I feel like the woman depicted on the lead coins all ghosts get is someone important in the big picture of the cosmology, anyone more into this that has some insight?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just feeling similarities. Lot of ways to play the correspondence.<br /> <br /> The woman could be the Stygian Oracle, the Dark Mother, Death herself, or any number of other things.<br /> <br /> Hell, it might be the one evidence we have of successful Catabasis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T21:43:21-07:00","id":1236293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236246#post1236246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hell, it might be the one evidence we have of successful Catabasis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would that maybe be the wife of Azar?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11057-sufferian","name":"sufferian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11057_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T22:18:03-07:00","id":1236302,"title":"","content":"I forgot to bring this up, but:<br /> <br /> The very clear implication about the link between Gates and geists, combined with the way Reapers work and the existence of the capacity for Tyranny in the bond of the Bargain, paints a very definite picture of how geists are treated differently between 1e and 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T22:55:08-07:00","id":1236310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sufferian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236293#post1236293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would that maybe be the wife of Azar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly, though given Iset's mythological line throughout the ages, one wonders how she would end up on something strongly associated with the Greeks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T23:19:26-07:00","id":1236315,"title":"","content":"I'm really liking the preview manuscript so far.<br /> <br /> The Krewe rule are great, and applicable to other splat's groupings like cabals, packs, motleys, etc. <br /> <br /> I was also contemplating how the Underworld and Reapers perceive and treat the undead like vampires and mummies. Do they consider them alive, dead, abominations? Do reapers need to &quot;return&quot; them to the Underworld, etc.?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T23:47:37-07:00","id":1236321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236315#post1236315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really liking the preview manuscript so far.<br /> <br /> The Krewe rule are great, and applicable to other splat's groupings like cabals, packs, motleys, etc. <br /> <br /> I was also contemplating how the Underworld and Reapers perceive and treat the undead like vampires and mummies. Do they consider them alive, dead, abominations? Do reapers need to &amp;quot;return&amp;quot; them to the Underworld, etc.?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires are dead, so the Underworld should see them as dead too. Mummies can't enter the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T00:45:38-07:00","id":1236331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236321#post1236321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires are dead, so the Underworld should see them as dead too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Counterpoint: Vampires are corpses, which the Underworld doesn't seem to have any use for. It's only interested in the ephemeral dead, not the debris left behind when they form. A Reaper might be mildly confused by this particular piece of debris walking around, but they would likely view them the same as the living counterpart to a Doppelganger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T00:45:47-07:00","id":1236332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1235926#post1235926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Descend is pretty frightening. I notice that it's listed as both a Manifestation and a Numen; is this intentional? The rules for each are just different enough to make me think it's not a typo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Descent and Engulf are both Numina. The Manifestation version should have been cut, but apparently I didn't scour the manuscript thoroughly enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T01:12:38-07:00","id":1236333,"title":"","content":"Is criticism permitted here? I expressed some <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/780017-how-long-will-the-kickstarter-for-c20-be-open-and-is-it-even-open-yet?p=784354#post784354\">misgivings</a> about the then upcoming Changeling 20 (which turned out to be correct) on that forum and got a two year ban.<br /> <br /> Has anyone complained about the use of the word &quot;trigger&quot; in chapter 3, like they did for the Brujah in the first V5 preview?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T02:56:22-07:00","id":1236343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236333#post1236333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is criticism permitted here? I expressed some <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/780017-how-long-will-the-kickstarter-for-c20-be-open-and-is-it-even-open-yet?p=784354#post784354&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">misgivings</a> about the then upcoming Changeling 20 (which turned out to be correct) on that forum and got a two year ban.<br /> <br /> Has anyone complained about the use of the word &amp;quot;trigger&amp;quot; in chapter 3, like they did for the Brujah in the first V5 preview?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I\u2019m aware of. (Is \u201ctrigger\u201d a troublesome word? I must be missing some context here.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T05:06:42-07:00","id":1236373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236333#post1236333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is criticism permitted here? I expressed some <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/780017-how-long-will-the-kickstarter-for-c20-be-open-and-is-it-even-open-yet?p=784354#post784354\">misgivings</a> about the then upcoming Changeling 20 (which turned out to be correct) on that forum and got a two year ban.<br /> <br /> Has anyone complained about the use of the word &quot;trigger&quot; in chapter 3, like they did for the Brujah in the first V5 preview?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because the term there is actually proper; the geist encounters something that causes it to panic and react instinctively. Forcing it to confront the damn thing and not being careful about it traumatizes it further and naturally results in it being a bit pissed off at you. This ties in with the idea that all geists are carrying a lot of emotional baggage. That, and the Brujah preview had some...other context I won't go into here. (Don't ask. Seriously, don't.)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a>: It's a psychological term for whatever provokes a PTSD reaction. Assholes have tried to use it for &quot;anything that offends anyone ever.&quot; So not necessarily, but as mentioned, in the right context it raises eyebrows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T05:15:48-07:00","id":1236376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236373#post1236373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, because the term there is actually proper; the geist encounters something that causes it to panic and react instinctively. Forcing it to confront the damn thing and not being careful about it traumatizes it further and naturally results in it being a bit pissed off at you. This ties in with the idea that all geists are carrying a lot of emotional baggage. That, and the Brujah preview had some...other context I won't go into here. (Don't ask. Seriously, don't.)<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>: It's a psychological term for whatever provokes a PTSD reaction. Assholes have tried to use it for &amp;quot;anything that offends anyone ever.&amp;quot; So not necessarily, but as mentioned, in the right context it raises eyebrows.</div> </div> </div> </div>The psych part I knew, \u201cAssholes have...\u201d part I didn\u2019t. Thanks. <br /> <br /> And indeed, geists have some serious issues. And I\u2019m actually glad they do - I feel Geist 2E is doing a good job of the \u201cghosts are people too\u201d angle, and your spiritual tenant who is a lesser death god too counting as a person, albeit a broken one at the moment, reinforces that for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T08:14:40-07:00","id":1236413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236321#post1236321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are dead, so the Underworld should see them as dead too. Mummies can't enter the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the thing is, the Underworld doesn't really have any effects on non-ghost dead. Only those with Essence can suffer Essence Bleed and get Trapped in the Walls. Chthonians damages ghosts through touch alone, but since it's because they commit ectophagia by doing so it can only affect ghosts. The Rivers damages only submerged or drinking ghosts, with no rules for how they interact with living or dead.<br /> Edit: You're either a ghost or you're not. Any effects of the Underworld either applies only to ghosts or to everyone indiscriminately of their state of deadness. This is notable because Bound are specifically considered dead, yet nothing in the Underworld affects Bound unless it also affects the living. The whole living/dead dichotomy is purely a 1e thing by now. It's technically possible we'll get more rules in later chapters, but I see no reason to split those rules over different chapters. Especially since we already have some Bound specific rules in the latest preview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 07-18-2018, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T10:19:51-07:00","id":1236459,"title":"","content":"Hey guys if I upgrade my pledge from 5 to 25 dollars, my reward will be upgraded too?<br /> And I'm not going to pay 30 dollars?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T10:45:50-07:00","id":1236474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236459#post1236459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys if I upgrade my pledge from 5 to 25 dollars, my reward will be upgraded too?<br /> And I'm not going to pay 30 dollars?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly correct","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T10:46:37-07:00","id":1236475,"title":"","content":"On the subject of the lady on the coins- my bet would be that she is Persephone, or perhaps Geshtinanna. You know, someone who actually enters and leaves the Underworld on a regular basis, and as such symbolize the transition from life to death.<br /> <br /> As for the connection between the Ocean of Fragments and Ocean Ouroboros- did you noticed that the former has the tendency to recess, while the later, according to the Guardians of the Veil, keeps on growing? More than that- do you remember that when the Abyss was at its lowest, the Ocean of Fragments was at its highest? I think we now know to where all those waters goes to, don't you think? And I must say it feels strangely appropriate to think about the Abyss growing so much that it eventually floods the world, only for another world to rise from its depths, clean from its previous identifiers, while a new Ocean now stirring at its depths. How many times did that cycle went before? And what if the gods of the world above are the same gods of the bellow? Or perhaps they are both the parts of the great Tiamat, the Dark Mother who was cut into two and had half of her body put high in the heaven, and one deep bellow the earth?<br /> <br /> You wanted a dread alliance of Scelesti and Reapers who work together to drown the world for a Geist/Mage crossover game? You have one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T11:40:15-07:00","id":1236496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236459#post1236459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys if I upgrade my pledge from 5 to 25 dollars, my reward will be upgraded too?<br /> And I'm not going to pay 30 dollars?</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as you switch to the reward you want. If you just upgrade without switching, it won't change your reward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T11:50:42-07:00","id":1236501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236376#post1236376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And indeed, geists have some serious issues. And I\u2019m actually glad they do - I feel Geist 2E is doing a good job of the \u201cghosts are people too\u201d angle, and your spiritual tenant who is a lesser death god too counting as a person, albeit a broken one at the moment, reinforces that for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love that feeling I've been getting throughout the Manuscript. 1st Ed geists were hinted to have stories and histories that you could search up but 2nd Ed is really showing how the Geists are mini death gods but low key having pretty sever identity criseses. Even the mini-death gods feel like people. And that is great and rich for storytelling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T12:19:18-07:00","id":1236509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236496#post1236496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As long as you switch to the reward you want. If you just upgrade without switching, it won't change your reward.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if I upgrade my pledge to 25 with the &quot;change&quot; button my reward will be the same for 5 dollars?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T12:58:10-07:00","id":1236523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236509#post1236509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So if I upgrade my pledge to 25 with the &amp;quot;change&amp;quot; button my reward will be the same for 5 dollars?</div> </div> </div> </div>You need to change your pledge tier. If you change it to the $25 tier, you get the $25 reward. If you only change the amount, it will remain at the $5 tier for rewards even if you increase the amount. It\u2019s the difference between \u201cI\u2019m backing this for $25\u201d and \u201cI\u2019m backing this for $5 and kicking in an extra $20.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T13:09:49-07:00","id":1236526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236523#post1236523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You need to change your pledge tier. If you change it to the $25 tier, you get the $25 reward. If you only change the amount, it will remain at the $5 tier for rewards even if you increase the amount. It\u2019s the difference between \u201cI\u2019m backing this for $25\u201d and \u201cI\u2019m backing this for $5 and kicking in an extra $20.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Although technically I think you can change that in BackerKit. But yes, you'll want to hit &quot;Manage My Pledge&quot; and select a new tier rather than just changing the amount. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T13:16:49-07:00","id":1236531,"title":"","content":"So with &quot;Manage my Pledge&quot; I'm going to change my reward too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T13:38:17-07:00","id":1236542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236531#post1236531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with &quot;Manage my Pledge&quot; I'm going to change my reward too?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep - if you click MANAGE MY PLEDGE, and then CHANGE MY PLEDGE, you should see the list of all reward tiers.<br /> If you select the Geist tier ($25), that becomes your reward tier and pledge amount. Your total will now be $25.<br /> <br /> Kickstarter only lets you select one reward tier, so whichever one you've selected should be it - it won't add multiple choices together, so no fears there.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the support!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22659-kickstarter-james","name":"Kickstarter James","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar22659_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T03:13:46-07:00","id":1236707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236373#post1236373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, because the term there is actually proper; the geist encounters something that causes it to panic and react instinctively. Forcing it to confront the damn thing and not being careful about it traumatizes it further and naturally results in it being a bit pissed off at you. This ties in with the idea that all geists are carrying a lot of emotional baggage. That, and the Brujah preview had some...other context I won't go into here. (Don't ask. Seriously, don't.)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a>: It's a psychological term for whatever provokes a PTSD reaction. Assholes have tried to use it for &quot;anything that offends anyone ever.&quot; So not necessarily, but as mentioned, in the right context it raises eyebrows.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do the Brujah have less emotional baggage, with a Beast that frenzies when threatened, hungry, or even insulted, exacerbated by the Clan curse? If anything the Brujah example is more psychologically appropriate, considering the Sin-Eater triggers include things like jealousy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T03:23:42-07:00","id":1236709,"title":"","content":"Man, I want to read the previews, but life\u2019s keeping me anchored fast. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236707#post1236707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do the Brujah have less emotional baggage, with a Beast that frenzies when threatened, hungry, or even insulted, exacerbated by the Clan curse? If anything the Brujah example is more psychologically appropriate, considering the Sin-Eater triggers include things like jealousy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The term being used right for one doesn\u2019t mean that it\u2019s being used wrongly for the other, so I don\u2019t understand why you\u2019d bring this up...?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Genuinely puzzled here, since I know hardly a thing about what\u2019s going on with V5 now (other than a lot of old timers hating it), nor particularly care. This is another forum after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 07-19-2018, 06:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T05:41:44-07:00","id":1236731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236707#post1236707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do the Brujah have less emotional baggage, with a Beast that frenzies when threatened, hungry, or even insulted, exacerbated by the Clan curse? If anything the Brujah example is more psychologically appropriate, considering the Sin-Eater triggers include things like jealousy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brujah didn't react to things that caused them to panic, or starvation. 'Triggered. You are offended by something in this scene and react to it with extrovert anger.'<br /> <br /> If you want to promote v5 you should probably do it in the appropriate forum, this is a completely different game with a completely different company and creators. If you want to argue with the people who complained about V5 you should probably find them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-19-2018, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T06:54:21-07:00","id":1236747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">link removed</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, instead of doing that here, can we indeed stay focused on Geist in the thread about the Geist's Kickstarter? Not saying that those discussions, doubts or whatever have no right to be, but here there's pretty much one of the CoD's underdogs having its chance to shine after almost a decade. I know because I was there waiting for this to happen. So please take any talk about the titan that's fucking Vampire: The Masquerade elsewhere.<br /> <br /> I'm just lurking in this thread, but that's a tangent that needs to die <i>now, </i>as far as this thread's concerned<br /> <br /> EDIT: And yes, I'm having a bad day and usually never reply like that. Happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 07-20-2018, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T06:57:18-07:00","id":1236748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236747#post1236747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, instead of doing that here, can we indeed stay focused on Geist in the thread about the Geist's Kickstarter? Not saying that those discussions, doubts or whatever have no right to be, but here there's pretty much one of the CoD's underdogs having its chance to shine after almost a decade. I knwo because I was there waiting for this to happen. So please take any talk about the titan that's fucking Vampire: The Masquerade elsewhere.<br /> <br /> I'm just lurking in this thread, but that's a tangent that needs to die <i>now, </i>as far as this thread's concerned<br /> <br /> EDIT: And yes, I'm having a bad day and usually never reply like that. Happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s Okay I do things I regret during bad days too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T06:58:13-07:00","id":1236750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236748#post1236748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s Okay I do things I regret during bad days too</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really regret that. The tone maybe, especially tomorrow, but I stand for the message.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T07:26:24-07:00","id":1236764,"title":"","content":"The Roanoke bit from Dark Ages Companion is in an upcoming stretch goal. What can people tell me about it? I have a player who loves history, especially local history, and we're based in the DC area. I think this might be a great hook for him into Geist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T07:34:09-07:00","id":1236769,"title":"","content":"Do animals sense if your a sin-eater?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T09:26:21-07:00","id":1236801,"title":"","content":"It's interesting to look at all the ways ghosts differ from other ephemeral beings and apply that clarity to the general systems of Manifestations and Influences as a whole.<br /> <br /> Like, Anchor being simultaneously the narrowest and most broadly-applicable of the common Manifestation Conditions underlines the ways in which ghosts are constrained \u2014 in addition to being defined by their living days, Anchor is <i>literally</i> &quot;a ghost can affect this specific thing as part of its Influence.&quot; The way Resonant works means that this is technically also true of spirits and goetia, but it also means that Infrastructure is especially odd as a Manifestation Condition even before the whole &quot;this Condition can be Created on behalf of another angel&quot; aspect \u2014 it makes geister and angels the only ephemeral beings whose Influences aren't necessarily tied directly to their baseline Manifestation Condition, and geister accomplish that through a more widespread access to the Open Condition instead of occult workings of unfathomable scale.<br /> <br /> Ghosts only suffering aggravated damage from banes in the unlikely event that they've Materialized, combined with the way their Essence recovery works, paints a real nasty picture of the consequences of ghostly violence (and especially ectophagia) in the Underworld, and it also brings yet more importance to the process of digging up information from old sources when memory-based Essence recovery still works and being Trapped in the Walls effectively triples a ghost's daily upkeep.<br /> <br /> It's also interesting to think about the way nonhuman ghosts add to the ghostly interaction with notoriety \u2014 sheer numbers make it more likely that the ghost of a cat or a car significant to a lot of people will be of higher Rank than a similar entity that was merely known of by a handful of people. (Do Barghests and Castoffs benefit from memory-based Essence recovery? I would assume so, considering they otherwise have minimal ability to use their Numina.)<br /> <br /> It plays neatly into things that there's such a stark dichotomy between ghosts in the living world and ghosts in the Underworld, even though in practice this is down to the living world having so much more to offer ghosts in contrast to the Underworld's Essence economy being more like the dog-eat-dog dynamics of the Shadow but with higher stakes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T09:55:24-07:00","id":1236810,"title":"","content":"When your Geist's rank increases (Dread Geist, resolving a Burden, Regalia, etc) do they also gain new traits as appropriate for their station? Can Regalia push them to Rank 6 if they are already Rank 5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T10:45:02-07:00","id":1236829,"title":"","content":"I believe it only caps off at 5. Doing other things that might normal raise it don't stack to bring it to 6 and beyond aside from DM discretion I guess, but by that point stats and traits might be a bit irrelevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T10:56:22-07:00","id":1236831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236829#post1236829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe it only caps off at 5. Doing other things that might normal raise it don't stack to bring it to 6 and beyond aside from DM discretion I guess, but by that point stats and traits might be a bit irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precedent from Werewolf suggests that a temporary bump to 6 might count for the purposes of banes but nothing else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T11:55:03-07:00","id":1236849,"title":"","content":"What's the Clash of Wills dice pool for Second Sight (and other innate Bound abilities)? Unlike the CoW sections in the other books GtSE doesn't even mention Attribute + Supernatural Advantage for non-dot rated supernatural powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T11:58:07-07:00","id":1236850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236829#post1236829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe it only caps off at 5. Doing other things that might normal raise it don't stack to bring it to 6 and beyond aside from DM discretion I guess, but by that point stats and traits might be a bit irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's likely, but wouldn't it just save word count to just put a cap in the Geist creation rules that Rank can't increase beyond 5 rather than putting that limit on almost all ways to increase Rank?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T12:24:11-07:00","id":1236856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236850#post1236850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's likely, but wouldn't it just save word count to just put a cap in the Geist creation rules that Rank can't increase beyond 5 rather than putting that limit on almost all ways to increase Rank?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically the way it's written in the book is that using Dread Geist and accomplishing Remembrance or Burden will only get you to Rank 5 instead of 6. Krewe regalia might be more ambiguous but I'd imagine getting to Rank 6 and beyond is more of just end game goals and accomplishment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T12:29:45-07:00","id":1236859,"title":"","content":"They have said that it's only 95% complete. But also it's pretty clear that Rank 6 ghosts were never human and 'ancient Chthonians and Kerberoi fall into this category.' 'When they appear in a chronicle at all, it's as plot devices.'<br /> <br /> Which doesn't imply it's a player option at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T12:35:45-07:00","id":1236862,"title":"","content":"page 126 of CofD core book says much the same about all ephemeral entities above rank 5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T16:40:18-07:00","id":1236945,"title":"","content":"About the krewe rules - they mention ways for a krewe to take lethal damage, but I can't find anything that does <i>bashing</i> damage to a krewe. Did I miss something or are all the sources of damage to a krewe lethal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T17:25:11-07:00","id":1236959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236945#post1236945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the krewe rules - they mention ways for a krewe to take lethal damage, but I can't find anything that does <i>bashing</i> damage to a krewe. Did I miss something or are all the sources of damage to a krewe lethal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably, just the instances listed happen to deal Lethal or Aggravated (though I have to recheck). They cover how fast Bashing damage heals, and something probably does Bashing damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T09:12:27-07:00","id":1237170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bashing damage indicates a general slipping of religious attitudes, observant but distracted from the faith by material concerns. </div> </div> </div>I think that the way to handle Bashing for Krewes is less specific sources of deliberate damage and more as a &quot;Shit happened this week. Take 1B to the Krewe.&quot; Or one of your celebrants is having a really bad time with life things. If they don't get help, you'll take 1B, so it's up to you if you want to spend a scene on figuring that out.<br /> <br /> If I'm right (I'm just guessing), then I'd expect this to come up in the Storytelling chapter. It feels loosely equivalent to a scene where your vampire goes feeding at the local nightclub. The analogue for a vampire feeding or a werewolf hunting, in Geist, is &quot;giving a shit about your congregation&quot;.<br /> <br /> The problem with my theory, of course, is that that damage goes away in two days so it doesn't really make sense as a penalty for failure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T10:52:03-07:00","id":1237198,"title":"","content":"A point of Bashing damage goes away in two days, but if the source is an ongoing problem (say, one of your celebrants is having trouble making her rent) then the situation may well keep dealing damage until you address it. And if more than one celebrant is dealing with stuff, or your krewe just asks a lot of them without every giving back, that could full up your damage track real fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T11:17:05-07:00","id":1237206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1237198#post1237198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A point of Bashing damage goes away in two days, but if the source is an ongoing problem (say, one of your celebrants is having trouble making her rent) then the situation may well keep dealing damage until you address it. And if more than one celebrant is dealing with stuff, or your krewe just asks a lot of them without every giving back, that could full up your damage track real fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>1B a day, even if it fades in 2 days, you will be gaining it faster than it goes away. Eventually, it is going to wrap around to more serious consequences.<br /> <br /> And that's not even factoring into taking more than 1 Bashing damage at a time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T19:24:43-07:00","id":1237366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1237206#post1237206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1B a day, even if it fades in 2 days, you will be gaining it faster than it goes away. Eventually, it is going to wrap around to more serious consequences.<br /> <br /> And that's not even factoring into taking more than 1 Bashing damage at a time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. It's a system where you can afford to ignore the NPCs of the krewe for a time, so the players can get up to Underworld hijnks or whatever. But you can't ignore them indefinitely or soon you won't have a krewe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T07:18:35-07:00","id":1237492,"title":"","content":"What happens if a vampire or a Mage loses his supernatural abilities in the Ocean of Fragments? Do you think it might be possible to lose the template?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15464-raphatheascended","name":"RaphaTheAscended","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T08:15:50-07:00","id":1237507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RaphaTheAscended</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1237492#post1237492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if a vampire or a Mage loses his supernatural abilities in the Ocean of Fragments? Do you think it might be possible to lose the template?</div> </div> </div> </div>It specifically calls out that vampires can return to human by loosing their identifiers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T08:46:37-07:00","id":1237514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1237507#post1237507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It specifically calls out that vampires can return to human by loosing their identifiers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. It's true, it's in preview 1. I let it go when I first read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15464-raphatheascended","name":"RaphaTheAscended","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T08:53:43-07:00","id":1237515,"title":"","content":"$17 away from Haunts in Memento Mori.<br /> <br /> Getting closer to 200% funded...<br /> <br /> EDIT: Annnddd, we have Haunts. A bit more to some additional PDFs, then a little to free Anthologies for (almost) everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-21-2018, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T09:24:37-07:00","id":1237988,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/geist-the-sin-eaters-2nd-edition/posts/2245054\" target=\"_blank\">New preview's up.</a><br /> <br /> Before I sing its praises, and there is a lot to praise, can I point out some errata that needs desperate fixing?<br /> <br /> We have:<br /> <br /> 1) No Tyranny rules, despite explicit Bound who use them,<br /> <br /> 2) Mr. Wong lacks a Ban,<br /> <br /> 3) Chapter 6 was posted twice.<br /> <br /> Apart from that, this is pretty damn cool! Reapers are more explicitly sympathetic than they were in the initial preview, even occasional allies (the spread of sample Reapers really helped; they're all people who come off as likable or otherwise human in some way), and for actually loathsome antagonists you can't go wrong with Eaters of the Dead.<br /> <br /> Also, can I say the idea of Weird Science Eaters is fucking hilariously awesome? I can't help but see the idea of Tesla Coil Plasm and think:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://media0.giphy.com/media/hokMyu1PAKfJK/100.webp\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T09:26:18-07:00","id":1237989,"title":"","content":"Brazil didn't won the World Cu,but you know what? We are in Geist: The Sin Eaters,and that's motherflipping better!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T09:41:20-07:00","id":1237993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1237988#post1237988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) No Tyranny rules, despite explicit Bound who use them,</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was really disappointed from this one- I'm really eager to see those, and how different they are from the Sin Eaters.<br /> <br /> And yeah, the ghost eaters are terrifying- far more than I expected them to be. I assume that eating ghosts would be scary, but they managed to give it a cannibalistic feeling I haven't thought they are going to have. On the other hand, considering the whole &quot;ghosts are people&quot; thing which is going on, I understand why they are presented that way. Eating a ghost is the same is eating a human- a sin against the world, and those who commit it should be just as terrible.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T10:46:18-07:00","id":1238008,"title":"","content":"Do Reapers' personalities change when donning their Deathmasks? It has been stated that different ghosts can, at different times, inherit (or obtain somehow) the same mask and they'll all technically be the same Reaper. But most descriptions seem to show that the Ghost donning the mask has a great deal of control while the Mask is on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T10:58:27-07:00","id":1238011,"title":"","content":"Can not Geists use the Death Mask? Can they become Reapers? And for human beings would be just normal Mementos?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":15464,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15464-raphatheascended","user":"RaphaTheAscended","date":". 07-23-2018, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15464-raphatheascended","name":"RaphaTheAscended","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T11:48:50-07:00","id":1238024,"title":"","content":"Do Kerberoi leave Deathmasks? Do Chthonians? Can you infuse Momentos with the waters of a river and over time make something like a Deathmask?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T12:01:33-07:00","id":1238027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1238024#post1238024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Kerberoi leave Deathmasks? Do Chthonians? Can you infuse Momentos with the waters of a river and over time make something like a Deathmask?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Nope, Geists.<br /> 2) Nope, Geists.<br /> 3) Nope, Geists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T13:06:26-07:00","id":1238040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RaphaTheAscended</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1238011#post1238011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can not Geists use the Death Mask? Can they become Reapers? And for human beings would be just normal Mementos?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so- geist's practically already &quot;wear&quot; a mask. Putting the corpse of another of their kind shouldn't have any effect, I think.<br /> <br /> And yeah, for the living (and the Bound, and anyone but a ghost) Deathmasks are simply elaborated, yet scary, mementos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T13:24:00-07:00","id":1238043,"title":"","content":"It should probably be made more clear, all it says is 'ghost' and that's used to refer to geists as well as lower-ranked entities in several places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T14:23:14-07:00","id":1238053,"title":"","content":"It should definitely be more clear. It doesn't just say &quot;ghosts&quot;. It says &quot;all ghosts&quot;. But then it also excludes Rank 1 ghosts for some reason. I know that they're unlikely to become Reapers due to their nature, but I really can't shake the feeling that a Reaper with surplus Deathmasks could very well give them to Rank 1 ghosts.<br /> <br /> Another discrepancy involving Rank 1 ghosts is that they don't become geists by drinking from a River. Drinking from a River only increases Rank by one, and geists start at Rank 3, but the fluff is quite clear that any ghost drinking from them is supposed to become a geist. If I'm wrong, then why are Rank 1 ghosts protected from being &quot;buried beneath a thick scum of Underworld-tainted Essence&quot; unlike Rank 2 ghosts when they drink from the Rivers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 07-23-2018, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T14:43:10-07:00","id":1238063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1238043#post1238043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should probably be made more clear, all it says is 'ghost' and that's used to refer to geists as well as lower-ranked entities in several places.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Let's not repeat the whole &quot;can ghouls use devotions&quot; argument :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T15:48:04-07:00","id":1238079,"title":"","content":"Mr. Wong has a five point merit that does not exist (Hoarder).<br /> <br /> As for Tyranny, it might show up in the storytelling chapter, like Catabasis and Catharsis. It is something players can do afterall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T15:59:24-07:00","id":1238084,"title":"","content":"This kind of thing might show up in the ST chapter as well but what <i>would</i> happen If Agathe Richter drank from a river while wearing the mask like she has contemplated? <br /> <br /> So far I would doubt that it would make a Kerberoi as at the moment my current thoughts are that Kerberoi are whole Krewe that create or suborn a Dominion and over time start to combine into the jumbled mass of plasm that they are. (Though, admittedly, a ghost wearing the carcass of another Geist who was a ghost that took in elements of the Underworld and again drinking from a (possibly different) river to take in more parts of the underworld does fit the ascetic of a combined <i>thing</i> with &quot;human&quot; origins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T18:06:56-07:00","id":1238100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1238053#post1238053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another discrepancy involving Rank 1 ghosts is that they don't become geists by drinking from a River.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're stuck in a loop and I don't imagine that's conducive to making the conscious decision to do something that <i>deals at least four points of aggravated damage to them </i>at the banks of a body of water that <i>dissolves their Corpus and is used as a migration route by consummate ectophages</i> in a place where hibernation is nigh-on a death sentence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-23-2018, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T20:00:26-07:00","id":1238112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1238100#post1238100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're stuck in a loop and I don't imagine that's conducive to making the conscious decision to do something that <i>deals at least four points of aggravated damage to them </i>at the banks of a body of water that <i>dissolves their Corpus and is used as a migration route by consummate ectophages</i> in a place where hibernation is nigh-on a death sentence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course not. It's still a discrepancy in the rules. Especially considering the myriad of ways to control someone's body or mind in CofD. Some of them being available for the Bound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T21:15:20-07:00","id":1238129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1238112#post1238112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course not. It's still a discrepancy in the rules. Especially considering the myriad of ways to control someone's body or mind in CofD. Some of them being available for the Bound.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a discrepancy that relies on contriving a ghost with arguably the second lowest odds of survival in the Underworld a full two layers down and then forcing them to do a thing that damages them and drains approximately half the Essence they could possibly have. That's not the kind of thing that merits attention in the core rulebook \u2014 that's <i>the very definition of an edge case</i>.<br /> <br /> It could conceivably be covered in the Companion or a later supplement, but &quot;what if the characters in a game whose default societal view is that the Underworld is a horrible dehumanizing machine decide to go far out of their way to commit an act of over-the-top cruelty in the name of answering a question of niche metaphysics&quot; is not what you call a <i>pressing matter</i>.<br /> <br /> Ditto &quot;what if one of the main movers and shakers in Underworld politics, empowered by a limited resource that necessarily requires the creation and utter destruction of a geist, gets ahold of more than one such resource and decides to give it to a ghost that doesn't realize it hasn't been the Roaring Twenties for nearly a century.&quot;<br /> <br /> A case can be made, given the shape of the question &quot;What's stopping communities of ghosts from forcing their pariahs to drink from the Rivers to get a resource?&quot; that both forms of Underworld empowerment call for a genuine (albeit not necessarily conscious at the surface) decision on the part of the ghost in question, like many other supernatural bargains in the setting \u2014 it's important to the narrative of the Reapers that they <i>chose</i> to take up the role of roving maw of the Great Below, and it's important that drinking from a River offers no other benefit to a ghost and several deterrents such that the Ranks of the dead are comparatively flatter in distribution next to, say, spirit courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T23:11:10-07:00","id":1238144,"title":"","content":"Different question: So, if a ghost claims a person, can they then put on the Deathmask to become a Reaper and correlate their results with the effects of Claiming, orrrr no?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T02:27:41-07:00","id":1238160,"title":"","content":"Am I the only one who feels weird at how it is plausible to spend 5 experiences on a dot of Synergy, expend that Synergy to make a memento...and not get those 5 experiences back? Or worse, have to spend even more experiences to own that three dot Memento merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T04:58:04-07:00","id":1238179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1238129#post1238129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a discrepancy that relies on contriving a ghost with arguably the second lowest odds of survival in the Underworld a full two layers down and then forcing them to do a thing that damages them and drains approximately half the Essence they could possibly have. That's not the kind of thing that merits attention in the core rulebook \u2014 that's <i>the very definition of an edge case</i>.<br /> <br /> It could conceivably be covered in the Companion or a later supplement, but &amp;quot;what if the characters in a game whose default societal view is that the Underworld is a horrible dehumanizing machine decide to go far out of their way to commit an act of over-the-top cruelty in the name of answering a question of niche metaphysics&amp;quot; is not what you call a <i>pressing matter</i>.<br /> <br /> Ditto &amp;quot;what if one of the main movers and shakers in Underworld politics, empowered by a limited resource that necessarily requires the creation and utter destruction of a geist, gets ahold of more than one such resource and decides to give it to a ghost that doesn't realize it hasn't been the Roaring Twenties for nearly a century.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> A case can be made, given the shape of the question &amp;quot;What's stopping communities of ghosts from forcing their pariahs to drink from the Rivers to get a resource?&amp;quot; that both forms of Underworld empowerment call for a genuine (albeit not necessarily conscious at the surface) decision on the part of the ghost in question, like many other supernatural bargains in the setting \u2014 it's important to the narrative of the Reapers that they <i>chose</i> to take up the role of roving maw of the Great Below, and it's important that drinking from a River offers no other benefit to a ghost and several deterrents such that the Ranks of the dead are comparatively flatter in distribution next to, say, spirit courts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they edge cases? Yes. Are they impossible? No. Will there be antagonistic Bound that could very well consider doing such things despite it not fitting with the default societal views? Well, if we've got rules for forcing your geist to commit cannibalism, forcing it to drink from Underworld Rivers, and even completely overrule your geists will and replace Synergy with Tyranny...<br /> I know these are not common occurences, but they're not impossibilities either. An inconsistency in the rules is still an inconsistency even if it's unlikely to show up during regular play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1238160#post1238160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only one who feels weird at how it is plausible to spend 5 experiences on a dot of Synergy, expend that Synergy to make a memento...and not get those 5 experiences back? Or worse, have to spend even more experiences to own that three dot Memento merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't yet know how easy or difficult it is to gain Synergy through completing Remembrances. But I do suspect three of the four automatic Synergy loss events to simply never be worth it. (The fourth one is being dying, which is worth it if the alternative is staying dead.) I also wish the reasons for Synergy loss wouldn't be described as clashing with the geist's subjective opinion that could theoretically agree with your actions, when Synergy loss applies universally. It makes a whole lot more sense to me saying that committing ectophagia to completion and drinking from the Rivers changes the very nature of your geist, and the foundation for your Synergy crumbles as you need to reconnect with it. That also fits better with the fact that you lose different amounts of Synergy depending on the Rank of the ghost you consumed.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Again, edge cases that shouldn't apply to PCs.</b></i> I just don't find &quot;that's rare and PCs aren't supposed to do that&quot; to be a satisfactory answer when rare exceptions are fun curveballs to throw at the players, and the rules equally applies to antagonists. PCs are always exceptional in their own stories, and so are many things they stumble over during their journey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T07:05:33-07:00","id":1238210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1238160#post1238160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only one who feels weird at how it is plausible to spend 5 experiences on a dot of Synergy, expend that Synergy to make a memento...and not get those 5 experiences back? Or worse, have to spend even more experiences to own that three dot Memento merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you did make the Memento, so you kinda own it already. I would give you the Memento merit as a freebie (and 0-2 XP back, to even things out, if making the Memento was significant).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T07:41:25-07:00","id":1238227,"title":"","content":"The Memento Merit (similar to other Merits in other gamelines that grants objects) reflects Mementos not gained through play. You certainly don't have to buy it if you create your own Memento or find one during play.<br /> <br /> But it brings up an interesting point. A Memento from the Merit can give you access to a Key you don't have and an effect based on that Key for 3 XP. A Memento created by yourself can only grant you a duplicate Key and the effect is as a result limited to being based on a Key you already have, and costs a trait dot worth 5 XP. You could technically trade it for a Memento with a Key you don't have, but then you're kinda trading away a part of yourself with a high cost that you must've felt proud over when creating it.<br /> The former is also protected by Sanctity of Merits if you lose it, while the latter is not. Depending on how resolving Remembrance works I might suggest as a house rule that a Vanitas that is destroyed refunds 3 XP (the same amount as the Merit; not sure if regular or Synergy type) to its creator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T08:46:18-07:00","id":1238240,"title":"","content":"Another option - what would be a decent 2-dot bonus to add to a Vanitas when held by its creator?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T10:13:41-07:00","id":1238265,"title":"","content":"There is <i>a lot </i>to b said about how many emotions Geist is creating in me,but holy christ,the Nursery just has to be the saddest thing to ever eappear in a onyx path book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T01:08:01-07:00","id":1238528,"title":"","content":"A question: do Bounds regain Willpower after a good night's rest in 2e? I don't think I've read it in the preview, and I know this is a mistake that's getting reprinted since Blood and Smoke...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Italian nuisance. English is my second language, so be patient!<br /> <br /> <b>My homebrew:</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/270766-domain-light-from-a-dead-star-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">[VtR 2e] Light From a Dead Star: Rome</span></a></b><br /> <a hr