n easily permitable variation of Dirge, as an aside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T12:51:50-07:00","id":1239413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1239345#post1239345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick Question, are ghost stairs climbable by Bound? What happens when you enter the second floor of a house that got burned down and left a ghost? Do bound look like their floating in the air on an invisible 2nd floor? Or are they hidden like a real wall would have?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you can touch a ghost...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T13:27:27-07:00","id":1239423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1239413#post1239413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if you can touch a ghost...</div> </div> </div> </div>If a Ghost stands in front of you, do you partially vanish from view from Living People?<br /> <br /> I think the obvious answer would be no and so the correlation being that Standing in a ghost building would look like a person floating. <br /> <br /> Buuuuutttt.... That's a bit more silly than I'd want to put in my game so I think, in my games, I'll just have people inside ghost buildings be invisible and hand wave any questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T15:39:09-07:00","id":1239460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1239423#post1239423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Ghost stands in front of you, do you partially vanish from view from Living People?<br /> <br /> I think the obvious answer would be no and so the correlation being that Standing in a ghost building would look like a person floating.<br /> <br /> Buuuuutttt.... That's a bit more silly than I'd want to put in my game so I think, in my games, I'll just have people inside ghost buildings be invisible and hand wave any questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. You wanna disappear, use Shroud. Otherwise, prepare to look like an idiot while ghosting about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T16:20:37-07:00","id":1239469,"title":"","content":"&quot;I'm walking on ghost-sunshine, yeah!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T16:24:45-07:00","id":1239470,"title":"","content":"So, if two doppelg\u00e4nger meet and one of them consumes another and becomes Rank 3 (as Rank 1 ghosts are unlikely to interact with each other) will that Rank 3 ghost still be &quot;buried beneath a thick scum of Underworld-tainted Essence&quot; despite essentially become more of itself and quite possibly reaching Rank 3 outside the Underworld?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T17:55:12-07:00","id":1239503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1239423#post1239423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Ghost stands in front of you, do you partially vanish from view from Living People?<br /> <br /> I think the obvious answer would be no and so the correlation being that Standing in a ghost building would look like a person floating. <br /> <br /> Buuuuutttt.... That's a bit more silly than I'd want to put in my game so I think, in my games, I'll just have people inside ghost buildings be invisible and hand wave any questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d just make it so the ghostly house became visible while they were inside to get around that. Unless I was going for funny, of course.<br /> \u201cDude, we need to go.\u201d<br /> \u201cI can barely hear you in here!\u201d<br /> \u201cLike, now! Come on!\u201d<br /> \u201cNot until I\u2019m done exploring this haunted house!\u201d<br /> \u201cThere\u2019s no house! Now stop flying at a third story level and let\u2019s get out of here!\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T19:05:53-07:00","id":1239528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1239503#post1239503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019d just make it so the ghostly house became visible while they were inside to get around that. Unless I was going for funny, of course.<br /> \u201cDude, we need to go.\u201d<br /> \u201cI can barely hear you in here!\u201d<br /> \u201cLike, now! Come on!\u201d<br /> \u201cNot until I\u2019m done exploring this haunted house!\u201d<br /> \u201cThere\u2019s no house! Now stop flying at a third story level and let\u2019s get out of here!\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;What are you doing? Pretending to be a mime?&quot;<br /> &quot;No, man, it's a ghost cage! I can't get out!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T20:03:49-07:00","id":1239536,"title":"","content":"I now believe all Mimes are Sin-Eaters frequently Doomed with the Stillness key with the Vine of Servant to cheer people up while they interact with ghost objects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T06:46:31-07:00","id":1239664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1239536#post1239536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I now believe all Mimes are Sin-Eaters frequently Doomed with the Stillness key with the Vine of Servant to cheer people up while they interact with ghost objects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm convinced that somewhere in France there's a Krewe consisting wholly of mimes out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T09:01:27-07:00","id":1239705,"title":"","content":"Goddamn, I love Reapers. They're probably my new favourite thing, but whenever I imagine one of them donning their Deathmask, I can only picture a Sailor Moon-style magical girl transformation. It's sort of the best mental image.<br /> <br /> Also, Agathe Richter is my waifu. She is the spectre haunting my heart - the spectre of communism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T08:26:58-07:00","id":1240447,"title":"","content":"Last 24 hours! Let's see if we'll manage to get another Stretch Goal before it ends!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T08:33:40-07:00","id":1240451,"title":"","content":"Is the Burden Aspiration supposed to be replaced after each time it's resolved? Chapter 3 describes it as a type of Aspiration so by RAW it would be replaced, but that would make maxing your geist's Rank way too simple. On the other hand, you really need a repeatable Synergy gain (other than buying with XP) for any of the willing Synergy loss examples to be tempting in the least.<br /> <br /> Edit: Is resolving Touchstones supposed to be able to bring your geist's Rank above 5? It seems unlikely but unlike most other ways to increase Rank there's no explicit cap at Rank 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T08:38:23-07:00","id":1240454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1240451#post1240451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Burden Aspiration supposed to be replaced after each time it's resolved? Chapter 3 describes it as a type of Aspiration so by RAW it would be replaced, but that would make maxing your geist's Rank way too simple. On the other hand, you really need a repeatable Synergy gain (other than buying with XP) for any of the willing Synergy loss examples to be tempting in the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine it to be a sort of very-long term Aspiration, similar to an Obsession to a degree.<br /> A Vengeful trying to undo the injustice that lead to his death might well be faced with the cyclopean task of Fighting Crime by tearing down corruption / stabilizing the local job market / provide real opportunity for the unpriviliged / give a voice to the voiceless. That will include a bit of trial and error and take a few chapters at least, imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T08:43:37-07:00","id":1240458,"title":"","content":"So- it looks like that chapter also lacks the Tyranny rules.. did I missed them in some earlier chapter, or something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T08:46:37-07:00","id":1240460,"title":"","content":"<b>James bell</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">From the development team:<br /> Tyranny, for the just the core rules, work as Storyteller-character Bound with a mechanical tag that says &quot;I'm a terrible person,&quot; which is all Sin-Eaters really need to know about them.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Use of Tyranny and further mechanics may come in future books, but nothing concrete beyond &quot;they're bad and become Storyteller characters&quot; is outlined at this time<br /> .</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#3D3D66\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">James bell</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">@Carl - yep, I'm there with you. I think if the &quot;see page XX&quot; had been removed from this draft, it would have saved a lot of questions. Hopefully, the creative team sees the interest and we have a really successful campaign ending, and future books could come out of that curiosity... (fingers crossed)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Apparently it wasn't supposed to be a thing.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","user":"reaperfrost8","date":". 07-30-2018, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T08:47:08-07:00","id":1240461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1239705#post1239705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Goddamn, I love Reapers. They're probably my new favourite thing, but whenever I imagine one of them donning their Deathmask, I can only picture a Sailor Moon-style magical girl transformation. It's sort of the best mental image.<br /> <br /> Also, Agathe Richter is my waifu. She is the spectre haunting my heart - the spectre of communism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always figured a sort of Vizared/Hollow thing from Bleach, personally. But I like the magical girls transformation sequence more - consider it imported into my headcanon.<br /> <br /> The spectre of communism made me lol. Now all you need is a professional artist/comedian/chronicler with a sentient Kangaroo as his Barghest Geist, which claims to have been active in Vietnam, who create a Krewe that tries to fight Capitalism with what amounts to pranks. (There is a German satirical book series called Kangaroo Chronicles dealing with something very similar - the Kangaroo is alive though.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T08:50:30-07:00","id":1240463,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/geist-the-sin-eaters-2nd-edition/posts/2250812\" target=\"_blank\">And the last preview is here!</a><br /> <br /> Tyranny rules have officially been forgotten in the mess, but everything else looks great! I love the Absent, whose hunger for Memories make them both terrifying monsters who often have sacrificed their own selves in the name of surviving another day and thieves of the most intimate, and pitiable, sympathetic protagonists because the alternative is <i>just that bad.</i> Also love the internal link they have to gaki (many Absent have learned how to eat corpses to absorb the last Memories of the recently deceased) and their core mechanic of Skill adaptation (an Absent's Skills are bound in their Memories; change Memories, change Skills. One coming back from a market is completely unpredictable, because you don't know what she's loaded today).<br /> <br /> The endgame options are all pretty cool too; I feel there's a point to be made about Catharsis being a part of Catabasis, becoming proof that there is a better way than the mad greed of the Chthonic, and it always ends with a pretty awesome final boss in the form of their Avatar, forced into being to engage a krewe in Titanomachy. Also, becoming a Chthonic God comes off as horrifying, easy, and...ultimately pointless, because what's it matter if the Reapers have visions of one more mad old tyrant? The Underworld just becomes more Underworld-y, at most. Still, if I ever get around to updating the Reality-Bending Horrors section of Second Sight, I am already planning on upholding the spirit of &quot;focus on the human!&quot; while breaking the letter; the main villain is indeed the Chthonic God the cult worships, because previously, the Chthonic God was its high priest. He has not changed in any way that matters; he's just more aloof and needs rituals to directly lead the cult now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T09:06:08-07:00","id":1240467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1240460#post1240460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>James bell</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">From the development team:<br /> Tyranny, for the just the core rules, work as Storyteller-character Bound with a mechanical tag that says &quot;I'm a terrible person,&quot; which is all Sin-Eaters really need to know about them.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Use of Tyranny and further mechanics may come in future books, but nothing concrete beyond &quot;they're bad and become Storyteller characters&quot; is outlined at this time<br /> .</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#3D3D66\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">James bell</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">@Carl - yep, I'm there with you. I think if the &quot;see page XX&quot; had been removed from this draft, it would have saved a lot of questions. Hopefully, the creative team sees the interest and we have a really successful campaign ending, and future books could come out of that curiosity... (fingers crossed)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Apparently it wasn't supposed to be a thing.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>What a cop out. Why even include rules for getting Tyranny in the first place? And part of those rules in the Cabeiros section? At least tell me they'll fix the Cabeiros section so it's even possible for Tyranny characters to achieve Cabeiros at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T09:11:00-07:00","id":1240468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1240463#post1240463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/geist-the-sin-eaters-2nd-edition/posts/2250812\" target=\"_blank\">And the last preview is here!</a><br /> ...<br /> Also, becoming a Chthonic God comes off as horrifying, easy, and...ultimately pointless, because what's it matter if the Reapers have visions of one more mad old tyrant? The Underworld just becomes more Underworld-y, at most. <br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I kind of liked that. (Actually I like that Geist has a few explicitly stated End-Games).<br /> <br /> Over all it seems like becoming one of the &quot;Chthonic Gods&quot; is basically like adding your own personality to an already troubled entity suffering from multiple-personality disorder or Schizophrenia. <br /> <br /> <br /> ....<br /> Wait... I just thought of something. Does that mean that, in a way, the Underworld (and it's Chthonic Gods that may or may not be the same thing as the underworld itself) can be thought of the same way a sin-eater thinks of Ghosts top-side? As a troubled individual(s) needing to be helped? <br /> <br /> <i>What happens if one or more krewes <b>succeeds</b> in helping the underworld itself to move on???</i><br /> <br /> I got to think on this, I smell a chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T09:23:09-07:00","id":1240472,"title":"","content":"Cabeiros is indeed terrifying- the fact that geists would always object to use it comes from the fact that it kinda destroys them, but I wonder why aren't there geists who, from their own will, try to rise to Rank 5+ and become Chthonic Gods by their own right.. I assume that such geists are simply not likely to offer a Bargain, and as such are not detailed.<br /> <br /> It just occurred to me that just the book is focused around those Bound which &quot;care for the dead&quot;, it also focus around those geists which &quot;care for the living&quot;. I assume that just as there are many Bound who exploit and torment the dead and their own geists for profit, there are geists which abuse and torment the living. A geist which offers the Bargain drank at least one time from the Rivers of the Underworld and said &quot;I had enough from this ***&quot;. A geist which wants to become a god can do so by forcing itself to swallow the dread water of the Underworld without reaching to the living, and would probably be an ancient and terrible monster which would defile the living in countless different ways. You want to know who the Chthonic Gods are? They are us, countless of selfish souls which devour others of their kind simply because they are too afraid of moving on, and prefer raw power over going to the next stage. The Chthonic Gods are afraid- and they keep on clinging to the world with tainted hands, leeching everything they can and sacrifice their own memories so they won't be forgotten by a world which cast them away. They are not the gods of death- they are dead gods, who wear masks in order to hide their own, terrified faces from themselves.<br /> <br /> Now, can we please, <i>please</i> get a Night Horrors book which details Tyranny based Bound, non friendly geists and unconventional Bargains? I mean, <i>please</i>...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 07-31-2018, 03:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T09:26:42-07:00","id":1240475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1240468#post1240468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wait... I just thought of something. Does that mean that, in a way, the Underworld (and it's Chthonic Gods that may or may not be the same thing as the underworld itself) can be thought of the same way a sin-eater thinks of Ghosts top-side? As a troubled individual(s) needing to be helped?<br /> <br /> <i>What happens if one or more krewes <b>succeeds</b> in helping the underworld itself to move on???</i><br /> <br /> I got to think on this, I smell a chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's more or less the point of Catabasis- you redeem at least a part of the Underworld, and make it a slightly better place than the life leeching terror it is. Do enough Catabas(i? ses? what is the right plural? is there a right plural?), and you'll save the Underworld from itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T09:38:50-07:00","id":1240479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1240460#post1240460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>James bell</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">From the development team:<br /> Tyranny, for the just the core rules, work as Storyteller-character Bound with a mechanical tag that says &quot;I'm a terrible person,&quot; which is all Sin-Eaters really need to know about them.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Use of Tyranny and further mechanics may come in future books, but nothing concrete beyond &quot;they're bad and become Storyteller characters&quot; is outlined at this time<br /> .</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#3D3D66\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">James bell</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">@Carl - yep, I'm there with you. I think if the &quot;see page XX&quot; had been removed from this draft, it would have saved a lot of questions. Hopefully, the creative team sees the interest and we have a really successful campaign ending, and future books could come out of that curiosity... (fingers crossed)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Apparently it wasn't supposed to be a thing.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Can they be a sidebar, though? I want to see what happens when the obviously unwilling geist is Unleashed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T13:55:57-07:00","id":1240573,"title":"","content":"So I'm skimming through the section on the Absent, and it keeps mentioning the Reap Memory numen, which I can't find in any of the manuscript sections. Am I missing something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T15:25:05-07:00","id":1240609,"title":"","content":"I don't really want Tyranny rules-I'm not going to play one, and for most game purposes I can just assume that it operates similar enough to Synergy that the only minor hack I might make is that Weakened Bond doesn't happen with casual Unleashings-so much as I want a <i>name</i> for those Bound who are Tyrants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T15:42:45-07:00","id":1240614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1240609#post1240609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really want Tyranny rules-I'm not going to play one, and for most game purposes I can just assume that it operates similar enough to Synergy that the only minor hack I might make is that Weakened Bond doesn't happen with casual Unleashings-so much as I want a <i>name</i> for those Bound who are Tyrants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, that sounds pretty good, given how their default endgame is becoming the ultimate tyrants of the Underworld. I would like to know if they actively need to browbeat their geists, which seems to be the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T15:58:20-07:00","id":1240623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1240614#post1240614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, that sounds pretty good, given how their default endgame is becoming the ultimate tyrants of the Underworld. I would like to know if they actively need to browbeat their geists, which seems to be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd play by the drama rule of thumb on that mostly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T17:56:46-07:00","id":1240659,"title":"","content":"A more significant issue re: Tyranny and Cabeiros: The final act is something that a character with Tyranny has ostensibly already done, and a character with Tyranny is the only sort that's remotely likely to succeed at the process leading up to the final act.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T02:13:09-07:00","id":1240770,"title":"","content":"Also is becoming a geist or reaper the only way to become rank 3+ ghost? What about previous books that had ghost at 3+ranks? Should they be treated retroactively made into geist? <br /> Or can Absent go up in rank without becoming either?<br /> <br /> Are rank 3 ghost that aren't geist none existent? Does this game just not care about pre-existing ghost of rank 3+?<br /> Is the bargain what makes the difference between a rank 3 ghost and a geist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T05:10:13-07:00","id":1240805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1240770#post1240770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also is becoming a geist or reaper the only way to become rank 3+ ghost? What about previous books that had ghost at 3+ranks? Should they be treated retroactively made into geist?<br /> Or can Absent go up in rank without becoming either?<br /> <br /> Are rank 3 ghost that aren't geist none existent? Does this game just not care about pre-existing ghost of rank 3+?<br /> Is the bargain what makes the difference between a rank 3 ghost and a geist?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually been answered; ghosts of Rank 3 and above automatically develop geist traits. Your Absent going up in rank is retiring your character, likely making a Bargain with your next one, because it's really hard to play a ghost who literally cannot make social attempts except to scare people. So yeah, all Rank 3+ ghosts who aren't Reapers (who aren't actually that Rank so much as borrowing it from their Deathmasks) should be treated as geists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T08:40:32-07:00","id":1240889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1240770#post1240770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also is becoming a geist or reaper the only way to become rank 3+ ghost? What about previous books that had ghost at 3+ranks? Should they be treated retroactively made into geist?<br /> Or can Absent go up in rank without becoming either?<br /> <br /> Are rank 3 ghost that aren't geist none existent? Does this game just not care about pre-existing ghost of rank 3+?<br /> Is the bargain what makes the difference between a rank 3 ghost and a geist?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a new edition so there are no pre-existing Rank 3 ghosts. No, Rank 3+ is the definition of being a geist. They're a subset of ghosts.<br /> Which makes Rank 2 doppelg\u00e4ngers committing doppelphagia quite interesting as they apparently turn into geists (with all which that implies) without any interference from the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T09:04:32-07:00","id":1240903,"title":"","content":"...and that's it. Kickstarter's over!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T10:20:49-07:00","id":1240930,"title":"","content":"I'm so glad that this Kickstarter managed to get as much funding as it did, and I can't wait to see all the cool things they come up with now that it's all set, but I'm a bit sad that the Geist Translation Guide was posted as such a late stretch goal, since we weren't able to make it quite that far, and it would make all of the great stuff in the pdf bundle slightly more relevant. Anybody else hoping it will still get made someday? I know I'll shout my support from the nearest rooftop if I have to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12318-gaius94","user":"Gaius94","date":". 07-31-2018, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12318-gaius94","name":"Gaius94","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T10:32:13-07:00","id":1240937,"title":"","content":"From what I can tell, and have read, &quot;Geist&quot; is just another name for any ghost that is Rank 3+. Not really a subset, more just a name to differentiate how &quot;other&quot; ghosts get at this level of power. <br /> <br /> Additionally, That's one of the things that I was unsure of:<br /> - On one hand, you can raise a ghosts rank through the aforementioned doppelphagia so theoretically &quot;merged doppels&quot; could get to rank 3+ this way (with everything that implies (keys, access to bargain, etc)<br /> - But on the other hand, it has been stated directly in the book that the only way to get to rank 3 is through a river of the underworld (though it may not have said only...). Which would indicate that there is a cap for Rank through any method other than drinking from a river (see exerpt below).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To increase Rank, a ghost must have the Experiences needed to buy both the Rank dot and purchase dots in Attributes, Numina, Manifestations, and Influences to bring herself up to the minimum for the new Rank as soon as it increases. Then she must drink from a River (p. XX.) If she survives, her player may spend the Experiences to raise Rank and buy the other attached Traits. </div> </div> </div><br /> But, throughout the book, I got the feeling that there are more Geists around both the Underworld and topside then in 1st Ed had. Like they're not the most common ghost you see but they're not uncommon. But, you know, the ones that know/learn &quot;Bargain&quot; is not all of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T10:45:34-07:00","id":1240944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1240937#post1240937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, throughout the book, I got the feeling that there are more Geists around both the Underworld and topside then in 1st Ed had. Like they're not the most common ghost you see but they're not uncommon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that feels consistent with &quot;Any person that passes the site of a burned-down bookstore from some 50 years ago, located at the disused 111 E. Memory Lane, catches the whiff of smoke from the site, then immolates in a flaming column, hearing a cackling laughter before finally dying.&quot; Geists and Reapers now seem to fill a similar niche to mid-Rank spirits in Werewolf as the primary occult troublemakers in their Earthly ecology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T10:50:23-07:00","id":1240951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius94</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1240930#post1240930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm so glad that this Kickstarter managed to get as much funding as it did, and I can't wait to see all the cool things they come up with now that it's all set, but I'm a bit sad that the Geist Translation Guide was posted as such a late stretch goal, since we weren't able to make it quite that far, and it would make all of the great stuff in the pdf bundle slightly more relevant. Anybody else hoping it will still get made someday? I know I'll shout my support from the nearest rooftop if I have to.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm hoping if the backerkit sales and additions bring it up over $117k, OPP will do the translation guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T16:36:47-07:00","id":1241067,"title":"","content":"There are preexisting rank 3 ghost. The Ka from a hollow Mekhet can be a rank 3+ ghost and they are 2E. Do they suddenly become a geist and incapable of causing social problems for the Mekhet?<br /> These are things that I have to worry about when using both geist and vampires on the same game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T16:52:47-07:00","id":1241074,"title":"","content":"I am very happy with the success on Geist 2e kickstarter! Now I'm going to find some old-fashioned keys and attach it to a keychain or as a pendant and wear it with pride for Geist!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22337-overcastghost","name":"OvercastGhost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar22337_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T17:00:20-07:00","id":1241076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1241067#post1241067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are things that I have to worry about when using both geist and vampires on the same game</div> </div> </div> </div>They really really aren't, because there's no way to get rid of the <i>Ka</i> and it only exists as a personal antagonist for a vampire \u2014 it is inherently an exceptional quality. &quot;The Ka is modeled as a Rank 1-5 ghost&quot; means &quot;the Ka exists with the stats of an ephemeral being of that Rank and can be interacted with by powers that can affect ghosts,&quot; not &quot;part of a Humanity 6- vampire drank from one of the Rivers of the Underworld, does so again at Humanity 4 and 2, and can <i>un</i>-drink from the Rivers if the Hollow raises their Humanity in addition to not being subject to any of the quirks of appearance that high-Rank ghosts tend to exist under or any variance in the complexity of its ban and banes based on that rating.&quot; It has no interaction with ghostly ecology besides inhabiting the same phase of Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T18:18:44-07:00","id":1241098,"title":"","content":"Rereading Haunts and boy howdy, there's nothing that's at all a setup for granting limbs and organs back to friends and families for a while with Tomb with the fact that the living and the dead can touch them, nope.<br /> <br /> &quot;Who gave you eyes like that...and said you could keep them?&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: As regards Shroud 3, remember kids: Puke THEN Possess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-31-2018, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T21:47:21-07:00","id":1241162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1240472#post1240472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You want to know who the Chthonic Gods are? They are us, countless of selfish souls which devour others of their kind simply because they are too afraid of moving on, and prefer raw power over going to the next stage. The Chthonic Gods are afraid- and they keep on clinging to the world with tainted hands, leeching everything they can and sacrifice their own memories so they won't be forgotten by a world which cast them away. They are not the gods of death- they are dead gods, who wear masks in order to hide their own, terrified faces from themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>You were their God?</i> Om managed.<br /> <i><u>Thousands were sacrificed. To the greater glory.</u></i><br /> <i>Can you hear me?</i><br /> <i><u>Thousands sacrificed greater glory. Me, me, me.</u></i><br /> <i>What was your name?</i> shouted Om.<br /> <i><u><a href=\"http://worsethanmanyfairies.tumblr.com/post/174200335745/dandibuja-who-are-you-said-om-the-small-god\" target=\"_blank\">Name?</a></u></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T21:56:13-07:00","id":1241167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1241162#post1241162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>You were their God?</i> Om managed.<br /> <i><u>Thousands were sacrificed. To the greater glory.</u></i><br /> <i>Can you hear me?</i><br /> <i><u>Thousands sacrificed greater glory. Me, me, me.</u></i><br /> <i>What was your name?</i> shouted Om.<br /> <i><u><a href=\"http://worsethanmanyfairies.tumblr.com/post/174200335745/dandibuja-who-are-you-said-om-the-small-god\" target=\"_blank\">Name?</a></u></i></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly &quot;here and now, we are alive!&quot; is the most apt motto for the bound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T23:12:06-07:00","id":1241184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1241067#post1241067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are preexisting rank 3 ghost. The Ka from a hollow Mekhet can be a rank 3+ ghost and they are 2E. Do they suddenly become a geist and incapable of causing social problems for the Mekhet?<br /> These are things that I have to worry about when using both geist and vampires on the same game</div> </div> </div> </div>Just as Mage Ghosts are not &quot;normal&quot; and don't follow the Integrity-to-Rank thing a mortal does, I would expect vampire ghosts to have *at least* as many special rules as, say, Dopplegangers or Cthonians should anyone making a Vampire book care to write them up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T05:59:24-07:00","id":1241267,"title":"","content":"Ka already have defined rules that describe them at all Ranks (and can actually be argued are pseudo-ghosts rather than actual ghosts as described in GTSE).<br /> No, I'm more concerned about Doppelg\u00e4nger (who are regular ghosts who happen to have a double) being able to reach Rank 3 without any input from the Underworld. Why do they become avatars of death without the influence of the Underworld instead of more of themselves (if that made sense)? Rank 1 Doppelg\u00e4nger might be the most common, but unless they're compelled to act outside their &quot;loops&quot; most Doppelg\u00e4nger committing &quot;doppelphagia&quot; would already be Rank 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T08:31:33-07:00","id":1241320,"title":"","content":"Forgive the odd question, but the Kickstarter payment went through for you? I got no confirmation of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T10:24:01-07:00","id":1241370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1241320#post1241320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive the odd question, but the Kickstarter payment went through for you? I got no confirmation of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but it can take several days for then to get to everyone. I think it took two to three days for my payment to process for an earlier Kickstarter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T12:34:59-07:00","id":1241451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1241267#post1241267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ka already have defined rules that describe them at all Ranks (and can actually be argued are pseudo-ghosts rather than actual ghosts as described in GTSE).<br /> No, I'm more concerned about Doppelg\u00e4nger (who are regular ghosts who happen to have a double) being able to reach Rank 3 without any input from the Underworld. Why do they become avatars of death without the influence of the Underworld instead of more of themselves (if that made sense)? Rank 1 Doppelg\u00e4nger might be the most common, but unless they're compelled to act outside their &quot;loops&quot; most Doppelg\u00e4nger committing &quot;doppelphagia&quot; would already be Rank 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just as a note, after rereading a few bits, I don't think it outside capability for a Rank 1 ghost to commit Ectophagia. Look at the ghost from &quot;A Brighter Morning&quot;. He seemed to fit the description of a rank 1 ghost. He was compelled into certain loops that he basically didn't have control over and had very limited ways of interacting outside of twilight. But all the same he was aware of himself (and seemed to understand he wasn't alive).<br /> <br /> I think Rank 1 ghosts may or may not know they're ghosts and also may or may not be compelled into loops that echo their death. But I don't think it's a hard rule (though the looping seems common, but again, that wouldn't preclude them from not knowing they're dead or at least being aware enough to be a person rather than an echo).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T17:19:12-07:00","id":1241577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1236212#post1236212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, as that goes, I won't personally settle for anything less than the absolute destiny apocalypse-nothing less than the absolute shattering of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Buuuuut baby steps.</div> </div> </div> </div>I share that sentiment. I wouldn\u2019t stop until I restructured the entire Underworld, not just sections. But that sounds like you would need a Conspiracy sized Krewe to accomplish something so ambitious... and I\u2019m not sure if it\u2019s feasible to get a krewe to that size in 2nd Ed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T18:03:14-07:00","id":1241601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1241577#post1241577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I share that sentiment. I wouldn\u2019t stop until I restructured the entire Underworld, not just sections. But that sounds like you would need a Conspiracy sized Krewe to accomplish something so ambitious... and I\u2019m not sure if it\u2019s feasible to get a krewe to that size in 2nd Ed</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotta start somewhere.<br /> <br /> And, if need be, franchise it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T18:19:04-07:00","id":1241608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1241601#post1241601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gotta start somewhere.<br /> <br /> And, if need be, franchise it.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201c Hello, I\u2019m with the Church of Unitology, have you heard of the word of Michael Altman?\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T19:16:37-07:00","id":1241627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1241608#post1241608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u201c Hello, I\u2019m with the Church of Unitology, have you heard of the word of Michael Altman?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;...The Reapers are <i>that </i>way.&quot; (slam)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T04:45:29-07:00","id":1241762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1241627#post1241627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;...The Reapers are <i>that </i>way.&amp;quot; (slam)</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually wanna a make a Krewe that follows the tenants of Unitology now, who try to save ghosts by returning them to fleshy bodies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T07:53:42-07:00","id":1241829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1172850-mage-2018?p=1173239#post1173239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had someone Awakening as they bled out after a suicide attempt, and came back alive and in their own body - but with a ghost of themselves bound to them as a Familiar. It was pretty interesting as the Ghost didn't have the ability to grow and change like the Mage ended up doing, and was always a reminder of what they'd moved through to get there.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Doppelgangers being a thing, now, my favorite Mage character's concept is actually a thing that can happen in the default setting.<br /> This is amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T00:47:17-07:00","id":1243143,"title":"","content":"I know it\u2019s something I\u2019ve brought up before, but the more I think on it the less I like the Memento creation process. It\u2019s not that it takes around a week to do at least, nor that it is stuck with one of your innate keys - those limitations are logical and can have some interesting moments behind them. It\u2019s the fact that a three experience merit is effectively being paid for by a five experience resource, Synergy.<br /> <br /> I appreciate that Synergy has means to be gained for free, but the fact that you a) lose supernatural tolernace, b) can actively lose experiences on this, and c) can lose something that is a reward for fulfilling a narrative feels...unsatisfying. There is no advantage for creating your own memento beyond the choice of hardware for it and having a personalized touch. You can\u2019t make ones that are stronger, nor gain keys you don\u2019t already have, and you\u2019re paying either two experiences more for the premium of a guarenteed chosen effect or you\u2019re spending a meaningful moment where you resolve either your own or your Geist\u2019s life. That\u2019s an awfully high downside to being able to make your own memento when you can just find the things at death sites, which Sin Eaters will be frequenting anyways.<br /> <br /> I also appreciate that Sanctity of Merits could apply, but it\u2019s hard to keep track of how much Synergy you\u2019ve paid for and how much you\u2019ve earned through gameplay, and as someone on Discord noted quite quickly, Sanctity of Merits only applies to Merits.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I\u2019m just too used to Demon or even Changeling, given how their own supernatural gadgets are usually more potent while also being cheaper to produce...though granted, mementos effectively being bulletproof is something neither splat can replicate with any form of ease, so that\u2019s one tradeoff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T02:29:38-07:00","id":1243153,"title":"","content":"The Rage Condition could need some clarification. &quot;Weapon rating&quot; is an extremely infrequently used term with no definition. Many take the weapon part to mean it makes your unarmed attacks deal lethal. Only two uses of the term (that I have found) has specified which damage type, which is lethal in one case and aggravated in the other.<br /> Others substite &quot;weapon rating&quot; with &quot;damage rating&quot; which is used to tell how much extra damage a successful attack does, but with no assumption about the damage type unless it's explicitly stated, which would mean bashing in this case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 08-06-2018, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T03:06:17-07:00","id":1243160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1243153#post1243153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Rage Condition could need some clarification. &amp;quot;Weapon rating&amp;quot; is an extremely infrequently used term with no definition. Many take the weapon part to mean it makes your unarmed attacks deal lethal. Only two uses of the term (that I have found) has specified which damage type, which is lethal in one case and aggravated in the other.<br /> Others substite &amp;quot;weapon rating&amp;quot; with &amp;quot;damage rating&amp;quot; which is used to tell how much extra damage a successful attack does, but with no assumption about the damage type unless it's explicitly stated, which would mean bashing in this case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't all weapons do Lethal in 2E, unless an exception is stated?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T03:48:15-07:00","id":1243164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1243160#post1243160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't all weapons do Lethal in 2E, unless an exception is stated?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but unarmed attacks aren't weapons. Does &quot;weapon rating&quot; turn your unarmed attacks into weapons? Or does it (like &quot;weapon modifier&quot;/&quot;damage rating&quot;) only describe the number of extra damage inflicted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T05:58:04-07:00","id":1243181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1243143#post1243143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it\u2019s something I\u2019ve brought up before, but the more I think on it the less I like the Memento creation process. It\u2019s not that it takes around a week to do at least, nor that it is stuck with one of your innate keys - those limitations are logical and can have some interesting moments behind them. It\u2019s the fact that a three experience merit is effectively being paid for by a five experience resource, Synergy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's why I wouldn't charge you an extra couple of XP for making a Memento. Also that Synergy has ways of being free to regain, something not that difficult to do with Remembrance. (Technically, that depends on the ST being willing to engage with the basic premise of the game, but..).<br /> <br /> Also, keep in mind a Memento always has at least one feature that makes them all extremely valuable; their Keys. Sin-Eaters cannot naturally form new Keys without ectophagia, something which involves murder and a loss of Synergy in it's own right-not to mention much more dangerous, since it's likely the geist who has that Key violently objects to being eaten. That's the reason the Merit is rather expensive; it's a new way of gaining both Plasm and Haunt variants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T06:03:49-07:00","id":1243184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1243181#post1243181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that's why I wouldn't charge you an extra couple of XP for making a Memento. Also that Synergy has ways of being free to regain, something not that difficult to do with Remembrance. (Technically, that depends on the ST being willing to engage with the basic premise of the game, but..).<br /> <br /> Also, keep in mind a Memento always has at least one feature that makes them all extremely valuable; their Keys. Sin-Eaters cannot naturally form new Keys without ectophagia, something which involves murder and a loss of Synergy in it's own right-not to mention much more dangerous, since it's likely the geist who has that Key violently objects to being eaten. That's the reason the Merit is rather expensive; it's a new way of gaining both Plasm and Haunt variants.</div> </div> </div> </div>That still doesn't cover the XP differential between &quot;Merit Bought&quot; Mementos and personally crafted ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T06:13:13-07:00","id":1243187,"title":"","content":"You can only increase Synergy a few times (four times, I believe) and after you've done that the game considers your character's story to be over.<br /> Regardless, the system is unbalanced in some way. Either Memento creation is too expensive due to Synergy dots being worth too much, or if they're not worth that much the XP cost for Synergy becomes too expensive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T07:09:19-07:00","id":1243199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1243187#post1243187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can only increase Synergy a few times (four times, I believe) and after you've done that the game considers your character's story to be over.</div> </div> </div> </div>You literally get a Synergy Beat for every time you resolve one of the Conditions a crisis point gives you, one of which has resolution criteria that amount to &quot;face another crisis point or raise your Synergy.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T08:15:34-07:00","id":1243211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1243199#post1243199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You literally get a Synergy Beat for every time you resolve one of the Conditions a crisis point gives you, one of which has resolution criteria that amount to &quot;face another crisis point or raise your Synergy.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that is not the issue. The issue is people are comparing creating a Momento in play vs purchasing one with/as a merit and the later is objectively* a better option.<br /> <br /> The issue has little to do with the ease of gaining Synergy, because a good Sin-Eater engaging in their own story should be trying to gain Synergy a lot. Compelling crisis points by conflicting the desires of the Bound and their geist should also be a frequently used way to lose said Synergy. That back and forth is the whole point until resolution is archived.<br /> <br /> Now the creation rules might be intended to prevent mass production of Momentos for krewe mates; So every Key belonging to the group is not availible to every member.<br /> <br /> *The merit soes not obey the limitation (which are noted as being flavourful) inheirent to the crafting process; you can aquire different keys with the merit (you can only create Momentos that share your inheirent keys). It cost less experience. It does not take as long to get ingame either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T08:58:24-07:00","id":1243221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1243211#post1243211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but that is not the issue. The issue is people are comparing creating a Momento in play vs purchasing one with/as a merit and the later is objectively* a better option.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is just a reversal of the usual trend where the merits were horrifically devalued compared to acquiring a Gadget/Grimoire/Artifact/Fetish etc in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T11:14:22-07:00","id":1243253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1243211#post1243211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but that is not the issue. The issue is people are comparing creating a Momento in play vs purchasing one with/as a merit and the later is objectively* a better option.<br /> <br /> The issue has little to do with the ease of gaining Synergy, because a good Sin-Eater engaging in their own story should be trying to gain Synergy a lot. Compelling crisis points by conflicting the desires of the Bound and their geist should also be a frequently used way to lose said Synergy. That back and forth is the whole point until resolution is archived.<br /> <br /> Now the creation rules might be intended to prevent mass production of Momentos for krewe mates; So every Key belonging to the group is not availible to every member.<br /> <br /> *The merit soes not obey the limitation (which are noted as being flavourful) inheirent to the crafting process; you can aquire different keys with the merit (you can only create Momentos that share your inheirent keys). It cost less experience. It does not take as long to get ingame either.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a bit of a white room scenario, but if a player stays with shaving half their starting Merit dots to start at Synergy 2, and then crafts a Memento of their own, tey\u2019re explicitely worse off than if they\u2019d simply started with the Memento merit at character creation. They\u2019d have the same amount of free reign in making the Memento, unless the ST was very limiting, but they\u2019d still have two extra merit dots and it could be of a Key they otherwise don\u2019t have access to.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the only advantage to crafting a Memento I can see is that you can choose what it is, have a choice over what benefit it has, and it will most likely have a Key that resonates with a strong attribute you have so you can reliably get a good amount of Plasm per Doom. Just finding Mementos through play/the merit are less likely to have desired efects or Keys tha resonate with a favored attribute.<br /> <br /> I do appreciate the thought that a Synergy cost would be a way to curtail a Krewe simply crafting enough Mementos to have the entire spectrum. The problem with that is, again, purchasing the merit doesn\u2019t follow that limitation beyond how they have the merit.<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s another concern; should a player craft a Memento, but they otherwise get the merit for free just as a way to account for the Memento. What would happen if that Memento were stolen, or otherwise permanently put out of the player\u2019s hands through no fault of their own beyond not making it harder to be lost in such a manner? They didn\u2019t pay experience for the merit, so Sanctity Of Merits doesn\u2019t apply...but they paid for it with Synergy, which may or may not have been paid for with long earned beats. How would you cover the disparity there?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1243221#post1243221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is just a reversal of the usual trend where the merits were horrifically devalued compared to acquiring a Gadget/Grimoire/Artifact/Fetish etc in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s quite the disparity, given that most of those only require between 1-5 experiences to craft yourself or, in a Demon\u2019s case, a Willpower dot that is replaced with an experience. Mementos require Synergy, which requires 5 experiences to raise manually. It\u2019s a weird tradeoff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 08-06-2018, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T11:14:55-07:00","id":1243254,"title":"","content":"The smart move for an absent is to claim a human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T12:01:49-07:00","id":1243262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1243254#post1243254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The smart move for an absent is to claim a human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of depends on what the Absent wants to do, plus if they have the manifestations for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T17:48:03-07:00","id":1243342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1243253#post1243253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s quite the disparity, given that most of those only require between 1-5 experiences to craft yourself or, in a Demon\u2019s case, a Willpower dot that is replaced with an experience. Mementos require Synergy, which requires 5 experiences to raise manually. It\u2019s a weird tradeoff.</div> </div> </div> </div>How much of this problem remains if the cost of the Merit is bumped up to five dots?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T17:54:15-07:00","id":1243344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1243342#post1243342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much of this problem remains if the cost of the Merit is bumped up to five dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>Greatly reduced but not completely; the lack of Sanctity is a big pain and there will always be those who complain about the limitation of the crafting process. On the whole, I think it would help a great deal. I don't think they feel like 5 dot merits though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T19:25:34-07:00","id":1243366,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd just be in favor of some smallish perk for Vanitas - would something like the 1E ability to summon you Keystone Memento fit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T21:05:30-07:00","id":1243389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1243344#post1243344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greatly reduced but not completely; the lack of Sanctity is a big pain and there will always be those who complain about the limitation of the crafting process. On the whole, I think it would help a great deal. I don't think they feel like 5 dot merits though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The weird thing is, a Memento is in certain respects and for certain purposes <i>better than</i> a dot of Synergy.<br /> <br /> 2e Geist's power structure is set up differently to, say, Vampire and Changeling, where the drawbacks of your condition start out easily manageable and gradually escalate with your power \u2014 the downsides of Synergy are instead front-loaded and remedied through either increasing your rating or dealing with separate elements that also raise your rating, and that combined with the lack of a separate Integrity analog means the power structure has allowances for &quot;weak&quot; veteran characters built into it in the form of Mementos and stolen Keys and progress along your geist's Remembrance.<br /> <br /> When it comes to Haunts, a dot of Synergy gives you an extra die, a better rate and capacity for spending Plasm, and a one-level bump to a few effects' numbers. That's the full extent of its impact on the things Mementos help with.<br /> <br /> A Memento, meanwhile, adds at least one die (and most likely two or more), gives you free Plasm that ignores the limits of capacity and rate, and potentially makes you more likely to get a refund on some of the Plasm you spent (even if it's Plasm that you didn't have until you used the Memento).<br /> <br /> Also, it's important not to sell duplicating one of your innate Keys short \u2014 you <i>can't unlock a Haunt with more than one Key at a time</i>, and you can explicitly push the free Plasm from multiples of the same Key through a given Haunt. (The debatably-minor occult power doesn't hurt, either.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T22:19:29-07:00","id":1243405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1243389#post1243389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The weird thing is, a Memento is in certain respects and for certain purposes <i>better than</i> a dot of Synergy.<br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to admit, I hadn't thought of all that before this point. It makes sense, and it does fit in with the limitation that making a new Memento has to be with your innate keys. It helps that the ability to downgrade damage via Plasm is unaffected by Synergy, so having multiple means of getting plasm is useful (though the ensuing Dooms may not be).<br /> <br /> However, increasing the cost of the merit from 3 to 5 experiences is...not exactly helping with the problem? All that means is that Mementos now cost even more to get on your character sheet, and 3 experiences isn't a light purchase as it is, much less 5.<br /> <br /> I don't know. Maybe I'm just the old man shouting at clouds for being over his lawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T23:23:00-07:00","id":1243414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1243405#post1243405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, increasing the cost of the merit from 3 to 5 experiences is...not exactly helping with the problem? All that means is that Mementos now cost even more to get on your character sheet, and 3 experiences isn't a light purchase as it is, much less 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't exactly trivial objects in the first place, particularly not in a game that introduced &quot;breaking points involving a magical item can give their subjects the Obsessed Condition&quot; and whose core societal mechanics are premised around Mystery Cult Initiation, the Merit whose minimal design notes include &quot;every one of these has a centering relic.&quot;<br /> <br /> Remember that the other means of getting these things consistently instead of relying on blind luck are &quot;bind a ghost into its own Anchor using a five-dot Ceremony&quot; or &quot;destroy a geist.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T01:10:20-07:00","id":1243427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1243414#post1243414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They aren't exactly trivial objects in the first place, particularly not in a game that introduced &quot;breaking points involving a magical item can give their subjects the Obsessed Condition&quot; and whose core societal mechanics are premised around Mystery Cult Initiation, the Merit whose minimal design notes include &quot;every one of these has a centering relic.&quot;<br /> <br /> Remember that the other means of getting these things consistently instead of relying on blind luck are &quot;bind a ghost into its own Anchor using a five-dot Ceremony&quot; or &quot;destroy a geist.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of us are accustomed to Magical Items being less valuable than dots of Supernatural Tolerance/ Integrity, which is likely where the perceived disparity comes from. <br /> <br /> To me, it seems Mementos are less closer to fetishes, Imbued Items etc (the \u201cutility items\u201d) and more closer to Athanors, Taliamans etc (the \u201cmilestone items\u201d). That\u2019d explain the opportunity cost in producing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 08-07-2018, 04:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T14:36:23-07:00","id":1243604,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts about Tyranny based Bound lacking proper name- do you think that &quot;Sacrosanct&quot; would work better as their nickname (taking inspiration from 1e), or could it be used for a new Krewe Archetype? I assume that Wretched (the proper 1e term for Synergy 0 Bound) also works, but it sounds to me more like how Sin Eaters would call such Bound, and not how those Bound would call themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T15:31:49-07:00","id":1243624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1243604#post1243604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some thoughts about Tyranny based Bound lacking proper name- do you think that &quot;Sacrosanct&quot; would work better as their nickname (taking inspiration from 1e), or could it be used for a new Krewe Archetype? I assume that Wretched (the proper 1e term for Synergy 0 Bound) also works, but it sounds to me more like how Sin Eaters would call such Bound, and not how those Bound would call themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can work with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T15:42:59-07:00","id":1243626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1243604#post1243604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some thoughts about Tyranny based Bound lacking proper name- do you think that &amp;quot;Sacrosanct&amp;quot; would work better as their nickname (taking inspiration from 1e), or could it be used for a new Krewe Archetype? I assume that Wretched (the proper 1e term for Synergy 0 Bound) also works, but it sounds to me more like how Sin Eaters would call such Bound, and not how those Bound would call themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Both</i> could work; they call themselves Sacrosanct because they see their own will and individuality, well, sacrosanct. They think they know better and are worth more than other people. They\u2019re called the Wretched by Sin-Eaters because first they\u2019re deplorable, and because Sin-Eaters see even them as people who were broken by a bad day and can be turned back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T15:45:07-07:00","id":1243627,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't Tyrants be an appropriate name? I mean I'm not apposed to Sacrosanct but I've just been calling them Tyrants.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Now that I think about it, I think that most of them just call themselves Bound and don't differentiate themselves with other Bound. Though I'm sure Sin-Eaters have a myriad names for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":654,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","user":"xiongrey","date":". 08-07-2018, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T15:51:05-07:00","id":1243630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1243604#post1243604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some thoughts about Tyranny based Bound lacking proper name- do you think that &amp;quot;Sacrosanct&amp;quot; would work better as their nickname (taking inspiration from 1e), or could it be used for a new Krewe Archetype? I assume that Wretched (the proper 1e term for Synergy 0 Bound) also works, but it sounds to me more like how Sin Eaters would call such Bound, and not how those Bound would call themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about, internally, Deathlords? They have (in their own minds) mastered (one of) the forces of Death, after all. And it sounds pompous enough for one who would crush another being's trust and remnants of humanity for their own desires.<br /> <br /> And it's not like the term is in use anymore from 1E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-07-2018, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T08:18:09-07:00","id":1243800,"title":"","content":"A bit of a bittersweet update today.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/geist-the-sin-eaters-2nd-edition/posts/2258516\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/2258516</a><br /> <br /> On the one hand, it is sad to see Travis step down.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Vera is awesome. Geist is in good hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T10:03:39-07:00","id":1243831,"title":"","content":"Well, I am officially sad. Travis did a great work in reshaping Geist into the awesome game it is. I am not saying his replacement won't do a good job either, but Travis made Geist more awesome than I could even imagine. Best wishes, Travis! May no mask trouble you in your path!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T11:40:14-07:00","id":1243860,"title":"","content":"We're sorry to see you go, Travis. Thank you for the wonderful book you've made for us!<br /> <br /> Welcome aboard, Vera. We look forward to the projects you will create!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":693,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","user":"ThomasM","date":".  Fixed punctuation 08-08-2018, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T12:27:31-07:00","id":1244244,"title":"","content":"For those with the preview document, I have a question about mementos. In the first edition, the different dot levels of the Memento Merit - charms/memorabilia, vanitas, fetters, and deathmasks - represented different types of object rather than just a power level. Is that still the case in the second?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T12:41:35-07:00","id":1244246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1244244#post1244244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those with the preview document, I have a question about mementos. In the first edition, the different dot levels of the Memento Merit - charms/memorabilia, vanitas, fetters, and deathmasks - represented different types of object rather than just a power level. Is that still the case in the second?</div> </div> </div> </div>All mementos are 3 dot merit, having a power and a Key. Greater mementos are some sort of urban legends, existing probably as higher rating (or N/A rating, probably) mementos. Deathmasks act as regular mementos, only that they work by wearing them, and that ghosts can use them to become Reapers, and they are not considered to be a part of the &quot;collection&quot; for memento collectors. Objects become mementos in all kinds of ways, as long as it includes the presence of residual death (or a Bound creating one by investing Synergy), but it doesn't effect the mechanical works of the item- they are still a 3 dot merits, with a power and a Key.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T15:02:06-07:00","id":1244281,"title":"","content":"As a quick note before expanding on this: The manuscript says that Deathmasks may be used (for purposes of a Sin-Eater using the key) by either wearing or holding the Deathmask. (Though it's it's not unlikely that the individual effect of the Deathmask requires wearing it).<br /> <br /> You've already been answered on this but I did want to expand a bit as I love the change. While there are different types of momentos, they're not referenced by dot number and for the most part they all have the following:<br /> - A Key (Keys are WAAY more important now)<br /> - A massively increased durability (so much to almost make them bulletproof depending on the object)<br /> - An effect (usually minor) that's (more or less) unique to that Memento (like being able to call the underworld when submerged, seeing in the dark only while standing still, or other smaller things).<br /> <br /> As for the different types of Mementos from 1st edition, they still exist (as was previously stated) and all have the above effects but may have shifted a bit from 1st Edition:<br /> - Charms: This word is't really used any more as all Mementos have a little effect to them regardless of origin.<br /> - Vanitas: These mementos only differ from other Mementos in that you created them. (they inherit your key and you (essentially) get to pick the item and effect). You have to sacrifice a dot of Synergy to do it but that is really it.<br /> - Fetters: While the word fetter still exists, it does not reference a Memento at all. Fettered ghosts are when a ghost decides to, essentially, possess an object. The spirit of the 1st Ed Fetter is something that is not uncommon for one of the main antagonists to do: The Eaters of the Dead. Basically, the spirit of the 1st Ed Fetter is pretty abhorrent to 2nd Ed Sin-Eaters.<br /> - Deathmasks: These are Mementos, but from a different origin (dead Geists). They work like any other Memento for the Bound but Ghosts using them turns them into the Reaper of that specific Deathmask. Also, using or even having them is pretty taboo in Sin-eater culture at large (note: sin-eater, not necessarily all Bound)<br /> - Memorabilia: Mementos created from a famous person or death do not inherently make them any different from any other memento. So there isn't a separate memento type for ones connected to famous people.<br /> <br /> And as a side note, the book says there could be other grander Mementos but you like, never see them. And if they're found, they're the kinds of things that Krewes go to war over. Things like the bones of Kerberoi with 4 keys. Or a physical object that has never been anywhere but the underworld till now that can allow the user to shift between twilight and physical at will. (I made up the examples as the book doesn't, but these are the kinds of things I imagine these chronicle based Mementos to be like).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":654,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","user":"xiongrey","date":". 08-10-2018, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T15:19:56-07:00","id":1244289,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar654_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"654\" data-vbnamecard=\"654\">xiongrey</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-01T2