_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1244281#post1244281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Fetters: While the word fetter still exists, it does not reference a Memento at all. Fettered ghosts are when a ghost decides to, essentially, possess an object. The spirit of the 1st Ed Fetter is something that is not uncommon for one of the main antagonists to do: The Eaters of the Dead. Basically, the spirit of the 1st Ed Fetter is pretty abhorrent to 2nd Ed Sin-Eaters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a small correction: The equivalent of the Fetters of 1e would be the Mementos created by the Ghost Binding Ceremony, which imprisons a ghost in an Ancora.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15464-raphatheascended","name":"RaphaTheAscended","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-02T06:16:26-07:00","id":1258527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1258510#post1258510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Is there somewhere we can see a quick recap of what it will include?</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at the Stretch Goal at Kickstarter has sections on: Mementos, Krewe Regalia &amp; Cerimonies, Dominions, Haunts, Haunted Locations &amp; Story Hooks. He also unlocked Chapter Fiction and Sample Krewes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15464-raphatheascended","name":"RaphaTheAscended","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-02T17:50:54-07:00","id":1258625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RaphaTheAscended</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1258527#post1258527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the Stretch Goal at Kickstarter has sections on: Mementos, Krewe Regalia &amp; Cerimonies, Dominions, Haunts, Haunted Locations &amp; Story Hooks. He also unlocked Chapter Fiction and Sample Krewes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds awesome! I'm reading the preview pdf in more detail and I must say I love what the game has become.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-04T20:26:43-07:00","id":1258994,"title":"","content":"Anyone else notice that Sin-Eaters can only get a full Willpower refresh once per <i>story</i> (per Anchor) instead of per session? O_o","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-04T22:47:19-07:00","id":1259015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1258994#post1258994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else notice that Sin-Eaters can only get a full Willpower refresh once per <i>story</i> (per Anchor) instead of per session? O_o</div> </div> </div> </div>Per-session is only a thing at all for Vampire and Changeling, and the nature of full refreshes is such that they usually aren't things it's advisable or possible to do very frequently in the first place. I'm similarly not too worried about it being the only gameline so far to put a frequency limit on single-point refreshes for non-mortal Anchors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-05T13:38:19-07:00","id":1259119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1259015#post1259015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per-session is only a thing at all for Vampire and Changeling</div> </div> </div> </div>And anyone with Virtue. Werewolf and Beast, meanwhile, have <i>no</i> frequency limit on full refreshes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-05T16:05:59-07:00","id":1259142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1259119#post1259119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And anyone with Virtue. Werewolf and Beast, meanwhile, have <i>no</i> frequency limit on full refreshes.</div> </div> </div> </div>So to be clear; mundanes, Mages, Demons, Ghosts, Angels, most 'minor' templates, Vampires and Changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-05T17:39:16-07:00","id":1259155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1259119#post1259119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And anyone with Virtue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figured that was implied by my contrasting against mortal Anchors in the very next sentence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Werewolf and Beast, meanwhile, have <i>no</i> frequency limit on full refreshes. </div> </div> </div>Neither does Promethean. Again, see &quot;usually not things that it's advisable or possible to do very frequently in the first place.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 10-05-2018, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T23:30:00-07:00","id":1259539,"title":"","content":"Unrelated to anything, behold, Bestow Regalia.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gJ03ajsAVcY\" data-code=\"gJ03ajsAVcY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/gJ03ajsAVcY/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> (I'm sorry-not-sorry)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T12:26:23-08:00","id":1265896,"title":"","content":"Has anyone heard of any Geist 2E character sheets in the works? I've been rereading the kickstarter manuscript and would love to see a visual of a character sheet <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T11:52:51-08:00","id":1271208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1259155#post1259155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figured that was implied by my contrasting against mortal Anchors in the very next sentence.<br /> <br /> Neither does Promethean. Again, see &quot;usually not things that it's advisable or possible to do very frequently in the first place.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I realise this is a bit of a necro, but... Mages effectively have two vices, as they regain Willpower through exceptional successes on their spells without any limits *as well* as having a mortal Vice.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T12:32:27-08:00","id":1271219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1271208#post1271208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I realise this is a bit of a necro, but... Mages effectively have two vices, as they regain Willpower through exceptional successes on their spells without any limits *as well* as having a mortal Vice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but by that metric vampires have no limits on Willpower recovery through gambling on frenzy resistance; pending previews to the contrary for Loyalty and Conviction in Deviant, every Anchor so far uses a core mechanic of &quot;you do this thing and you get Willpower&quot; with no specific need for rolled actions. Spellcasting's relation to Willpower recovery (particularly through Praxes) is closer to Vampire's use of the Predatory Aura as a vector for the Inspired Condition than it is to a standard Vice \u2014 the latter doesn't usually <i>require</i> a good roll to land.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T05:52:20-08:00","id":1271959,"title":"","content":"Reading over the effects of the caul I realised that mixing a few of the vitiate abilities from the caul would allow a sin eater to turn into a shoggoth with enough plasm. Sin eaters are truly the most terrifying of all supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T05:54:35-08:00","id":1271960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1271959#post1271959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading over the effects of the caul I realised that mixing a few of the vitiate abilities from the caul would allow a sin eater to turn into a shoggoth with enough plasm. Sin eaters are truly the most terrifying of all supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's that 'with enough Plasm' bit that trips you up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T06:02:57-08:00","id":1271961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1271960#post1271960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's that 'with enough Plasm' bit that trips you up.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a high tyranny bonepicker antagonist I was working on who is all to happy to commit ectophagia once he traps an entire town in a blizzard that won't be the biggest problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T09:23:41-08:00","id":1271998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1271960#post1271960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's that 'with enough Plasm' bit that trips you up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Max out some Attribute and get a lot of Keys for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T09:45:27-08:00","id":1272005,"title":"","content":"Have a Key with an Unlock Attribute at 3 or more dots. Unlock a Haunt with that Key for one Plasm, spend another Plasm to ignore the Doom, and get more free Plasm than you just spent. Cancel the Haunt and repeat ad infinitum for literally infinite Plasm and all you need is to have an Unlock Attribute at 3+.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T12:56:02-08:00","id":1272027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1272005#post1272005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have a Key with an Unlock Attribute at 3 or more dots. Unlock a Haunt with that Key for one Plasm, spend another Plasm to ignore the Doom, and get more free Plasm than you just spent. Cancel the Haunt and repeat ad infinitum for literally infinite Plasm and all you need is to have an Unlock Attribute at 3+.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://www.quickmeme.com/img/ed/ed1d530c3894f49cfcf43b01a30c08c74f4131a579862139f689edaa671d4bd2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T18:06:08-08:00","id":1272091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1272005#post1272005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have a Key with an Unlock Attribute at 3 or more dots. Unlock a Haunt with that Key for one Plasm, spend another Plasm to ignore the Doom, and get more free Plasm than you just spent. Cancel the Haunt and repeat ad infinitum for literally infinite Plasm and all you need is to have an Unlock Attribute at 3+.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Just use your magical death-powers constantly&quot; is never going to be a trivial thing. Also, &quot;cancel the Haunt&quot; isn't a thing \u2014 Haunts end when their Conditions do, which largely means you have to be <i>using them</i> to get the Plasm back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T05:25:49-08:00","id":1272154,"title":"","content":"It's mechanically trivial to activate them and most if not all of them are trivially easy to end their Conditions prematurely. Often by spending the single charge you paid Plasm for.<br /> I have heard that this loop will be changed in the released version just because it's so easy to abuse, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T07:05:03-08:00","id":1272169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1272154#post1272154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's mechanically trivial to activate them and most if not all of them are trivially easy to end their Conditions prematurely. Often by spending the single charge you paid Plasm for.</div> </div> </div> </div>On <i>doing things</i>. You're not getting returns from singing the Dirge to empty air for three seconds or extruding the Caul to ignore wound penalties you aren't suffering or consulting the Oracle about absolutely nothing. This is a storytelling game that is played with other people \u2014 the rules are written under the implicit assumption that you're going to use them in a way that makes sense with what's happening in the story and not waste the other players' time on inconsequential activity in the name of raw numbers. Using a supernatural power is not a trivial act in a game where supernatural powers are a narratively significant element of the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have heard that this loop will be changed in the released version just because it's so easy to abuse, though. </div> </div> </div>Yes. That is my <i>point</i>. Even if there weren't a clear distinction between refilling your Synergy-derived Plasm capacity with cyclical use of Haunts and having the necessary stock to actually funnel dozens of points' worth of Plasm into Enhancements in a single application, &quot;You can abuse this blatantly exploitative reading of the mechanics if you're willing to completely ignore self-evident design intent and treat the game's representation of above-average Attribute ratings as unexceptional&quot; is a poor attitude to bring into a discussion of the game.<br /> <br /> You lose excess Plasm from Keys at the end of the scene and buying off the Doom before Synergy 6 limits your gains to three Plasm per use. When your &quot;trivial&quot; application of the mechanics to use nearly the full Plasm capacity of a starting character calls for using the same power on nothing three times in a row before actually doing anything with it, it's time to take a long hard look at your approach to RPGs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T08:32:23-08:00","id":1272184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1272169#post1272169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You lose excess Plasm from Keys at the end of the scene and buying off the Doom before Synergy 6 limits your gains to three Plasm per use. When your &quot;trivial&quot; application of the mechanics to use nearly the full Plasm capacity of a starting character calls for using the same power on nothing three times in a row before actually doing anything with it, it's time to take a long hard look at your approach to RPGs.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's trivial not because it's something you can do under pressure, but because you can do it whenever during downtime or even between Scenes without any consequences, as currently written. And above-average Attributes are unexceptional for PCs since it's literally impossible not to start with at least one Attribute at 3+. The majority of players prefer their characters to be competent so they'd prefer to choose Keys that are unlocked with their highest Attributes.<br /> (Not to mention that the Storytelling System has an inherent problem in trying to map dot ratings to competence due to the ridiculous ease with which you can start with above average dot ratings as well as the ease of increasing them during play. Players are mechanically incentivised to ignore the dot rating chart and play exceptional characters due to the lack of &quot;failing forward&quot; mechanics as well as Exceptional Successes being one of the most common XP sources. This is one of the inherent flaws of the system that have become more and more apparent during my years of playing CofD games.)<br /> <br /> And my approach to RPGs? I think they messed up big time by including an obvious infinite Plasm loop directly above the intended mechanism for gaining free Plasm through Keys that always imparts the Doom. I'm <i>glad</i> this obvious exploit is getting fixed. <i>Now stop assuming things about my thought process or attitude towards RPGs.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T09:20:04-08:00","id":1272190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1272005#post1272005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have a Key with an Unlock Attribute at 3 or more dots. Unlock a Haunt with that Key for one Plasm, spend another Plasm to ignore the Doom, and get more free Plasm than you just spent. Cancel the Haunt and repeat ad infinitum for literally infinite Plasm and all you need is to have an Unlock Attribute at 3+.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this was said to be changed to spend 1 FV instead of Plasm to ignore the Doom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15464-raphatheascended","name":"RaphaTheAscended","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T09:25:14-08:00","id":1272191,"title":"","content":"The obvious close to the loop seems to be doing like Demon does with the Compromise from Exploits - spend a Willpower to eliminate the roll. Here, spend a Willpower to eliminate the Doom. Willpower is a bit harder to game as quickly, and isn't directly part of the system, so that should work.<br /> <br /> I mean, then it just becomes a Willpower-to-Plasm conversion engine, with increasingly more efficient gains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 12-01-2018, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T22:04:42-08:00","id":1272304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1272184#post1272184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's trivial not because it's something you can do under pressure, but because you can do it whenever during downtime or even between Scenes without any consequences, as currently written.</div> </div> </div> </div>And even as currently written <i>you cannot break the per-turn limit without using the Plasm from Keys</i>. &quot;You can fill your pool during downtime&quot; is not an argument against the loop any more than it is for Vampire or Mage \u2014 being able to have a full pool at the start of a fresh scene has not historically been a problem for these games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And above-average Attributes are unexceptional for PCs since it's literally impossible not to start with at least one Attribute at 3+. </div> </div> </div>You are continuing to ignore the point I am making about the narrative half of ludonarrative elements in the name of raw mechanics and I'm not sure how you think that argument connects in any way with &quot;characters who can buy off the Doom of a Key through unlocking Haunts and still make a net gain in Plasm are doing so through aspects of their abilities that an average character could not be assumed to have the same competence in, so if you're leaning real hard into the fact that you own the Book of the Burn Ward or first died by burning as a means of topping off your reserves of ghost snot then you've probably got a good head on your shoulders.&quot; 3+ dots in an Attribute doesn't have to be hard for a PC to have for it to be a meaningful thing about the character relative to other characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is one of the inherent flaws of the system that have become more and more apparent during my years of playing CofD games. </div> </div> </div>Congratulations. I could not care less what you have to say about the flaws of the system in this context, where my issue is that you are here refusing to approach points of clear design intent in good faith because the Kickstarter draft mechanics don't explicitly forbid you from using a deliberate loop mechanism for long-term fuel recovery in a way that looks narratively bonkers to act out as a means of rapid short-term fuel recovery in this <i>storytelling game</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Now stop assuming things about my thought process or attitude towards RPGs.</i> </div> </div> </div>I'll be clearer, then:<br /> <br /> <i>Stop acting like arguments based around abusive readings are relevant or helpful in a discussion that is not framed with the intent to ask about how one could abuse the mechanics.</i> The context you decided to drag it back up in was &quot;if you load up on Plasm-intensive Enhancements of a mid-level Caul then you could be an unholy terror, but that is trickier than it sounds.&quot; &quot;Not if I do a shitty thing!&quot; is a shitty response to make to someone making the second phrase's observation as a rider to the first, and if that doesn't have anything to do with your thought process or attitude toward RPGs then it more than doesn't belong in the discussion, it <i>extremely</i> doesn't belong in the discussion.<br /> <br /> &quot;The loop can be exploited&quot; was brought up during the Kickstarter and the book is currently well out of the writing and editing stages at this time \u2014 it's not new information and nobody reading this thread will be in a position to do anything about it until the advance PDFs go out. There is no reason to keep picking at it at this stage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1272191#post1272191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The obvious close to the loop seems to be doing like Demon does with the Compromise from Exploits - spend a Willpower to eliminate the roll. Here, spend a Willpower to eliminate the Doom. Willpower is a bit harder to game as quickly, and isn't directly part of the system, so that should work.<br /> <br /> I mean, then it just becomes a Willpower-to-Plasm conversion engine, with increasingly more efficient gains.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is the matter of &quot;just tapping a Key to get a free kicker of Plasm offers no way of avoiding the Doom&quot; being a distinct mechanic that ought to remain relevant as a narrative device \u2014 a simpler method might be to limit buying off the Doom to once per instance per story so that there's still an incentive to collect additional Keys even without a lack of direct necessity for cycling through available instances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-02-2018, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T08:52:36-08:00","id":1272394,"title":"","content":"I'm not impressed with the argument from narrative significance. People are <i>real good</i> at rapidly turning wondrous discoveries to mundane practical use. As a species we figured out flight a little over a century ago. Airplanes are pretty damn phenomenal but ask most people who use them what they think and you're almost certainly going to hear about what a hassle security is, or how uncomfortable the seats are. Hell, we can have a real time video conversation from hundreds of miles away using two assemblies of plastic, metal and glass, and that's just a normal thing for a lot of people. Expecting people to not use magic powers for stupid exploits is expecting people <i>to not act like people</i>.<br /> <br /> 3 in an attribute isn't at all uncommon and it isn't just a PC problem. Very, very few of the published NPCs restrict themselves to even starting character stats, where it's impossible to have fewer than two such attributes. The majority have significantly higher values than that. Yeah, most aren't supposed to be &quot;average&quot; people, but even the ones that are often have three, four or even five attributes at 3+. When literally every PC and NPC significant enough to have a stat block is above average 3 dots does not feel out of the ordinary. They can make the claim that it is all they want, that's not how they treat it when it's time for examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T16:59:22-08:00","id":1272486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1272394#post1272394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not impressed with the argument from narrative significance.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm not impressed with &quot;Let's assume that an exploitative out-of-character reading of the mechanics is how the in-universe applications of what those mechanics represent are supposed to go for literally nothing judging from a draft copy&quot; on the list of nonsensical bad-faith arguments, but here we are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Expecting people to not use magic powers for stupid exploits is expecting people <i>to not act like people</i>. </div> </div> </div>I'm not proposing Sin-Eaters are never going to use their deathly powers in the name of convenience. I'm saying that <i>the end-state of the published game is probably not going to be written for &quot;Bob the Bound invites his geist Bubonica into his flesh repeatedly, leveraging his high Stamina and Key of Sickness to recover Plasm in the process of doing literally nothing but turning a power on and off&quot; to be a part of the world as encountered</i>.<br /> <br /> A character who is using a Haunt is using it <i>for something</i>. That is why the recovery loop is <i>a loop</i> and not <i>a point that says &quot;Sin-Eaters with the right combination of Keys, Haunts, and Attributes refill their Plasm between scenes without consequence or remark.&quot;</i> The people with magic powers in this hypothetical are not doing a stupid exploit, they are <i>engaging in nonsensical behavior that they would only arrive at through out-of-character knowledge of the way the game is written in a particular iteration of the rules</i>.<br /> <br /> A character is not going to conclude that the thing they should do is merge with their geist for enhanced physical plasticity, do nothing, dismiss their geist from their body, and then do this again three to six more times without the presupposition that your borrowed powers can be tapped for literally no reason except to cram what would be multiple scenes' worth of gradual sipping at the power of the Underworld into a laughably short timescale.<br /> <br /> The loop is made such that you're incentivized to use Keys with Haunts so that you can get more effect out of them with the Plasm that you're drawing from them, and most Haunts are minimally things you have running for a scene. If you are refilling your stocks in this fashion, it is pretty definitely intended to be comparable to the returns you would get from rolling an exceptional success in a resonant scenario or accepting the Doom to not need to lower your net gains by two Plasm. It's very clearly <i>not</i> made to have characters Unlock their favorite version of the Caul and then dismiss it five times in one scene for a top-off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When literally every PC and NPC significant enough to have a stat block is above average 3 dots does not feel out of the ordinary. They can make the claim that it is all they want, that's not how they treat it when it's time for examples. </div> </div> </div>Shockingly, most characters significant enough to have a stat block are not examples of run-of-the-mill NPCs like you'd pick off the street at random. &quot;This Attribute is one of your stronger points&quot; does not change just because most fully-statted NPCs aren't rocking a full spread of ones and twos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-02-2018, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T12:58:41-08:00","id":1272677,"title":"","content":"The closest to fulfilling the needs for the loop in any way that makes narrative sense is sitting around masturbating while under the effects of the Caul, which a) is a waste of a Haunt, and b) sounds less like the kind of thing that you do at the table and more like some kind of short fiction that you might write. Odds are it will not be particularly gripping fiction.<br /> <br /> In game, a lot of exploitation loops of this sort don't make sense for characters who just quite frankly have shit to do-characters don't know they are gaining EXP by doing these things, and so it takes a very <i>odd</i> mindset to make it justified.<br /> <br /> Out of game, it's basically a masturbation effort that slows up the game unless everyone is into it, in which case why not just say &quot;fuck it&quot; and give people all the EXP they need for the character they are satisfied with and just go on with it.<br /> <br /> Exp and other resources are there to incentivize their characters to go and do interesting things. It is therefore safe to assume that any reading of the rules that leads to the story basically grinding to a halt and resulting in boring slogs is an inherently faulty one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-03-2018, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T15:37:17-08:00","id":1272716,"title":"","content":"And here we go again with the farcical &quot;Characters can't see their character sheet, which means that they are somehow incapable of using simple observation to gain a rudimentary understanding of how things work&quot; Before the internet it's not like we could just look at a cheat sheet for fundamental constants of physics whenever we wanted. That didn't stop us from figuring out how to put them to work for us. Hypothetical Bob here doesn't start switching a power on and off completely at random, that <i>would</i> be nonsense. He uses a Haunt with a Key for a reason, and thinks &quot;Huh, I got more plasm out of that than I put in. I wonder if that happens every time?&quot; He doesn't know that he has 6/10 plasm or whatever. He doesn't <i>need</i> to know the specific numbers that his player does. He just has to possess a <i>modicum </i>of observational awareness to realize he has a bit more reserve than he did, and then possess enough curiosity to experiment and see if the effect is repeatable. <br /> <br /> This isn't some weird combination of merits from multiple game books that have an unintended synergy that players can exploit, this is a basic part of the Sin Eater experience that characters have plenty of reason and opportunity to encounter. At least some of them are going to do the very human thing of trying stupid nonsense just to see what happens. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1272486#post1272486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shockingly, most characters significant enough to have a stat block are not examples of run-of-the-mill NPCs like you'd pick off the street at random. &quot;This Attribute is one of your stronger points&quot; does not change just because most fully-statted NPCs aren't rocking a full spread of ones and twos.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's some convenient selective quoting you have going there but I'm going to be clear and repeat myself: <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Yeah, most aren't supposed to be &quot;average&quot; people, <u><i><b>but even the ones that are often have three, four or even five attributes at 3+. </b></i></u> In fact, of the five books I checked, LITERALLY EVERY ONE.<br /> <br /> I'm not looking in the high end antagonist Night Horrors books either. I'm talking Autumn Nightmares, which manages to have a True Fae who's weaker than most of the changelings (somehow) didn't field a single human with less than three attributes at 3 or more. Not a high power book. Largely generic &quot;patrol officer&quot; and &quot;gang banger&quot; from Hurt Locker, same story. None of the sample characters in the 2e core either. This is obviously far from a complete survey of NWoD/CofD books but again, can't find a single example. Can you point to even one NPC who doesn't have at least two &quot;exceptional&quot; attributes? Can you even find one who doesn't have three?</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T16:03:19-08:00","id":1272719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1272716#post1272716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And here we go again with the farcical &quot;Characters can't see their character sheet, which means that they are somehow incapable of using simple observation to gain a rudimentary understanding of how things work&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not farcical for characters to treat engagement with supernatural powers that come with a cost as something to be interacted with carefully, and to make that argument is likewise not engaging with the point under discussion:<br /> <br /> &quot;Characters who use a Key to Unlock a Haunt and don't put all the Plasm they got from doing so into the Haunt can produce a net gain in their Plasm reserves provided they still end the scene without more Plasm than they can normally hold,&quot; &quot;spending an extra point of Plasm when using a Key to Unlock a Haunt allows them to do so without suffering that Key's Doom,&quot; and &quot;the Caul is a Haunt whose effect can be dismissed essentially at will,&quot; taken as a set of <i>unfinalized mechanics</i>, do not paint a picture that suggests the exploitative combination of those three things will survive to the publication date when the same set of mechanics also includes &quot;a character can gain free Plasm from using a Key without Unlocking a Haunt by willingly suffering a Doom&quot; and &quot;a character who rolls an exceptional success on activating a Haunt with a Key receives half the Plasm they spent on it \u2014 even if it was Free Plasm \u2014 when the Haunt's Condition ends without resolving.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's far more likely that either a stipulation will be added to the free Plasm gained from Unlocking or the exemption toll will be removed than it is that this\u2026<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have a Key with an Unlock Attribute at 3 or more dots. Unlock a Haunt with that Key for one Plasm, spend another Plasm to ignore the Doom, and get more free Plasm than you just spent. Cancel the Haunt and repeat ad infinitum for literally infinite Plasm and all you need is to have an Unlock Attribute at 3+.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026is going to be Good Advice That Will Last The Ages And Not Get You Nasty Looks At The Table From People Who Came To Make A Story About Ghost-Talkers. It is not a defensible perspective in a discussion about the things limiting how much Plasm you can pour into a single application of a Haunt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you point to even one NPC who doesn't have at least two &quot;exceptional&quot; attributes? Can you even find one who doesn't have three? </div> </div> </div>Again: You're jumping from &quot;having three dots in an Attribute represents that character being above-average in that trait&quot; to &quot;characters the book uses to represent meaningful points of interaction that require the detail of a full sheet aren't average or below-average in any way because they have any Attributes at three dots or higher.&quot;<br /> <br /> The stats for a minion-type Horror have the equivalent of Attribute 2 + Skill 2 + Specialty for their best rolls. A mid-tier Retainer rolls the equivalent of Attribute 2/Skill 2/Specialty/Area of Expertise in their field of focus. Both roll less than four dice for anything else. These are characters possessed of competencies that are unremarkable, regardless of any bone you have to pick with using the books' fully-defined example characters as a measuring stick for what the system treats as &quot;average.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T16:17:25-08:00","id":1272722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1272719#post1272719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Every single Sin-Eater that you will meet in the game is already a noteworthy character, and will be guaranteed to have exceptional traits as a result. Does it even matter that there are theoretical Sin-Eaters with unexceptional stats if you'll never encounter them in the game?<br /> <br /> 2. I haven't replied to this thread in three days. I'm pretty sure that means you can Stop Shitting On Me Since I'm Obviously Not Interested In Participating In This Discussion And Found It Preferable To Leave Rather Than Arguing With You.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T16:44:45-08:00","id":1272724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1272677#post1272677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...sitting around masturbating while under the effects of the Caul, which a) is a waste of a Haunt, and b) sounds less like the kind of thing that you do at the table and more like some kind of short fiction that you might write. Odds are it will not be particularly gripping fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>gripping</i> fiction</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/DduwlDoUwAAKUFP.jpg:large\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","user":"Cielle","date":". 12-03-2018, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T16:52:22-08:00","id":1272726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1272722#post1272722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Every single Sin-Eater that you will meet in the game is already a noteworthy character, and will be guaranteed to have exceptional traits as a result. Does it even matter that there are theoretical Sin-Eaters with unexceptional stats if you'll never encounter them in the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>By the arguments presented, any starting player character will have at least six Attributes in which they are not above-average. It very definitely matters that not every character has stats that make any given Key equally viable for perpetuating a low-spend Unlock loop, because, again, those <i>are</i> most of the characters you'll encounter in the game, optimization be damned; a character with high Composure but no innate Stillness Key or a Grave-Dirt Key and low Strength is just as valid as the high-Stamina paragon of the Key of Disease or the high-Presence bearer of a Bloody Memento.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. I haven't replied to this thread in three days. I'm pretty sure that means you can Stop Shitting On Me </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure the fact that I went out of my way to not quote the thing you said that started this argument in a way that would put it in your Notifications in the course of reminding a different person who picked up your argument what the words I was arguing with were can be safely taken as a sign that my continued participation in the argument has very little to do with you as a person, much less &quot;shitting on you.&quot;<br /> <br /> You said a thing that I disagreed with on the basis of its promoting undesirable play habits and I would be content to leave it at that if people would stop defending it as at all reflective of the game's presented milieu. I did not make HelmsDerp take your argument and extend it into an argument about the in-universe viability of a mechanical hiccup in the incentives for using Keys while conveniently forgetting what &quot;cancel the Haunt and repeat&quot; means in relation to the practice of using unspent Free Plasm to refill to capacity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T22:14:08-08:00","id":1272781,"title":"","content":"...anyways.<br /> <br /> According to tonight's MMN, Memento Mori has moved to Redlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T23:33:36-08:00","id":1272789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1272781#post1272781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...anyways.<br /> <br /> According to tonight's MMN, Memento Mori has moved to Redlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*whistles*</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-04T11:25:01-08:00","id":1272868,"title":"","content":"Every day Memento Mori gets further in production the more I lurk to look for hints and teasers of what those new Haunts in the book will be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-04T12:46:48-08:00","id":1272873,"title":"","content":"I can't promise Haunt spoilers, but since I anticipate I'll need to change a fair number of Ceremony names, we might make a tease for them out of the rejects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T00:34:38-08:00","id":1273680,"title":"","content":"I hope the 'unlimited power loophole' gets patched in editing. I don't think it needs more than a sidebar paragraph saying don't do this but that would go a long way with disrespectful players trying to pull a rules lawyer act.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T06:49:56-08:00","id":1273709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1273680#post1273680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope the 'unlimited power loophole' gets patched in editing. I don't think it needs more than a sidebar paragraph saying don't do this but that would go a long way with disrespectful players trying to pull a rules lawyer act.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to suspect a more thorough shift, either in terms of a time or use limit on the Free Plasm gained from Unlocking a Haunt or in terms of cutting out the buy-off option altogether, because as it stands the ability to completely circumvent the risks of two similar long-term gains processes for the price of a single point of Plasm kind of chops the legs out from under angling for resonant Haunt use or tapping a Key directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T20:59:25-08:00","id":1274828,"title":"","content":"is It ok if I ask what this loophole exactly is? sounds like it was a very huge balance problem","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T22:26:05-08:00","id":1274837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1274828#post1274828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is It ok if I ask what this loophole exactly is? sounds like it was a very huge balance problem</div> </div> </div> </div>This is going to take a bit of diagramming to explain despite its simplicity, so bear with me:<br /> <br /> Like most of the other gamelines, Geist offers a lot of ways to get its fuel source, with different methods having different costs and drawbacks, but the loophole in question is a bit of a slant on the intent behind Keys.<br /> <br /> Basically, if you have a Key innately or through a Memento, you can use it to get free Plasm in one of two ways: tapping it to Unlock a Haunt (making it more effective in the process), or directly drawing upon the Key for Plasm without using a power. At its most basic level, both of these require you to accept the Doomed Condition for that Key, preventing you from using it again until you resolve the Doom by suffering its effects or helping a ghost whose death resonates with it to pass on. In both cases, using a Key gives you Plasm equal to your dots in the linked Attribute, but Unlocking a Haunt requires you to use the Haunt and therefore spend at least one point of Plasm.<br /> <br /> Rolling an exceptional success on a Haunt you unlocked with the Key (which is easier when you use it on a resonant target or circumstance) means you don't suffer the Doom and get back half the Plasm you spent on the Haunt if its requisite Condition ends without being resolved by contact with your Ban or Bane, which is there to encourage you to use the free Plasm you get from Unlocking a Haunt with a Key whose Attribute is one you have a high rating in both liberally and in resonant circumstances.<br /> <br /> Simply tapping a Key for Plasm, meanwhile, gives you the full payout with no surcharge, which is why the Doom is non-negotiable.<br /> <br /> Where this gets fucky is that you can get the same Doom-averting benefit on Unlocking a Haunt without rolling an exceptional success by spending an extra point of Plasm, and as-written the draft does not specify that you have to spend the free Plasm you get from Unlocking on that Haunt or on any sort of timescale; the only limits of Free Plasm are that if you have more than your Synergy-based capacity at the end of the scene any excess is lost, so you can top yourself off with impunity by spending as little as needed to use a Haunt and avoid the Key's Doom.<br /> <br /> What this means, in other words, is that it's safer and more consistent to get a Key whose Attribute is one in which you have at least three dots, use it to Unlock a Haunt at the minimum level of effectiveness and buy off the Doom for two points of Plasm, and repeat from scene to scene than it is to actually engage with that Key's resonant elements or tap the Key without using a power, despite this effectively translating to rewarding completely inconsequential use of deathly powers and artifacts more effectively than slinging buckets of ghost snot around or inviting misfortune upon yourself to steep yourself in the energies of death.<br /> <br /> Needless to say, it's <i>probably</i> against design intent for asserting telekinetic control over a small rock or briefly merging with your geist to offer better returns on Keys than taking on a temporary curse or funneling Plasm through your system in service of thematically relevant uses of Haunts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T15:55:08-08:00","id":1274975,"title":"","content":"iirc, the devs have said that it'll change from spending plasm to ignore the doom to something like spending willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"ht