ars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T17:15:08-08:00","id":1355723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1355716#post1355716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which one? I originally had a lot of little nods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant the one to <i>Grace Hunts In Hollywood</i>, though I have an inkling you may have been behind Mama Crow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T17:39:04-08:00","id":1355727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1355723#post1355723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant the one to <i>Grace Hunts In Hollywood</i>, though I have an inkling you may have been behind Mama Crow?</div> </div> </div> </div>All of the Regalia and Ceremonies Chapter is my messy baby. Apologies about the messiness, by the way-the entire process was riddled with a lot of things happening, definitely the roughest period I've written in so far.<br /> <br /> On that note, Vera has final say, but after evaluating the changes and tweaking the values based on the final product, here's what my take on it was*:<br /> <br /> Furies<br /> Bloody Mary Done Me Wrong: 1-Dot<br /> Boulevard of Winters Lost: 3-Dot<br /> Law Writ in Blood: 5-Dot<br /> <br /> Mourners<br /> Play It Forward: 5-Dot<br /> Extended Checkout: 1-Dot<br /> DJ Amadeus's Sick Flow: 3-Dot<br /> <br /> Necropolitans<br /> Come As You Are: 4-Dot<br /> L'amour du Vide: 2-Dot<br /> My Twenty Dollar Cherubim: 3-Dot<br /> <br /> Pilgrims<br /> Losing the Religion: 1-Dot<br /> Tripitaka's Journey: 3-Dot<br /> Running with Atropos' Scissors: 5-Dot<br /> <br /> Undertakers<br /> For Those Who Are Left: 1-Dot<br /> What's Old is New: 2-Dot<br /> Walking the Destroyer's Path: 4-Dot<br /> <br /> *Now mind you, that's with me being a little shaky on the nature of temporary anchors and how to balance that against how some ceremonies are more regular practice and others are grand rituals and honestly that I just basically went wild on the ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T19:40:24-08:00","id":1355745,"title":"","content":"I really like the Void Haunt, though I'm not sure what sort of dicepool people are meant to be making with their Void 2 ranged attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T21:36:24-08:00","id":1355759,"title":"","content":"Some real dope mementos in the set. The Honeyed Mourning Cloth seems neat for reasons I can't articulate.<br /> <br /> Glad to see Cassini made it to the final cut. Also enjoying the formula for the krewe archetypes' opening paragraphs.<br /> <br /> Curious what the &quot;natural&quot; end state is for the Void and the Well, given that I can presently find no way for the Haunt-standard exceptional success effect to actually kick in, but they're definitely flavorful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T22:50:10-08:00","id":1355776,"title":"","content":"While I don\u2019t agree with that, any storyteller can make any mechanical in game effect work, I do admit that the opportunity to actually make use of it is .. difficult at the very best of times.<br /> <br /> But I have noticed something about Well that is very rare for the Chronicles of Darkness: it can give a single player character the means to plunge the living world into utter ruin if the \u201cRight\u201d River has been supped from.<br /> <br /> The River of Life specifically. It\u2019s waters recede and are used up each time a bit of it is imbibed, bringing its waters into the living world would be an irresistible, and extremely irresponsible temptation to indulge. Even though these waters don\u2019t linger, the power of the River is still being used, so it is still being depleted.. what do you suppose would happen if a misguided Sin-Eater tries to use his new connection to the River to heal the masses?<br /> <br /> The Void can be devastating, but that damage is more often than not going to be highly localized. With the River of Life, the havoc one could unintentionally cause is much, much further reaching.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 12-19-2019, 01:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T09:25:09-08:00","id":1355870,"title":"","content":"Does the Doppelganger created by Bloody Mary Done Me Wrong cease to exist once the Duration expires, or does it merely lose the Aspirations provided by the Ceremony? If it's the former, that seems... really messed up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T16:30:27-08:00","id":1355962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1355870#post1355870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Doppelganger created by Bloody Mary Done Me Wrong cease to exist once the Duration expires, or does it merely lose the Aspirations provided by the Ceremony? If it's the former, that seems... really messed up.</div> </div> </div> </div>As opposed to creating a new person to fulfill a purpose and then left to suffer ghostly Twilight and the Underworld without an actual Anchor? I was writing for Sin-eaters, not mages.<br /> <br /> The Sin Doppelganger is a Meeseeks. It lives to enjoy it's purpose and then moves on having fulfilled equanmity by terms of the occult rules of the Ceremony. It would be cruel for it to persist beyond the confines of the Ceremony's intent.<br /> <br /> NOW, Boulevard of Winter's Lost is actively a ritual for assisted suicide that <i>will</i> challenge your Synergy, and Law Writ in Blood is totally an excuse to enact a Cabin In The Woods ritual (perhaps a bit kinder).<br /> <br /> I didn't quite execute it, but I did intend for at least a third of the Ceremonies to push the boundaries of what Sin-Eater Krewes would find comfortable. The route to the throne of heaven may not inherently kill virtue along the way in Geist, but that's not to suggest it doesn't <i>try</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-19-2019, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T19:59:09-08:00","id":1355990,"title":"","content":"Just wondering about this but does the void haunt permanently kill a sin eater if hes killed by it or can he resurrect as usual?<br /> <br /> Seeing as it mentions that being consumed by it means that theres no escape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T04:18:33-08:00","id":1356038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1355990#post1355990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just wondering about this but does the void haunt permanently kill a sin eater if hes killed by it or can he resurrect as usual?<br /> <br /> Seeing as it mentions that being consumed by it means that theres no escape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the wording and the implications of the fluff, it seems that the Void will consume Sin-Eater and Geist whole, which you kinda need your Geist to bring you back to survive.<br /> <br /> So yes, it seems to be a perma-death thing no matter the current Synergy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Consumer of lore, myth, history, tales and songs. Pronoun ambiguous. <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#9b111e\">This isn't gonna be easy, but the fact that you're even trying says a lot about you. You're braver than you think.</span></b></i> --RWBY V5C5","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25357-lorekeeper","name":"Lorekeeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T07:05:34-08:00","id":1356292,"title":"","content":"Can I say I found a lot of the Dominions humorous?<br /> <br /> Neon Table seems to be a place where the Bouncer is awfully chummy for a Keberos, being her own gatekeeper and also having gendered pronouns, but as horrifying as it is given context, there's just something incredibly amusing about the mental image of a Sin-Eater begging not to affix the bartender uniform upon them.<br /> <br /> &quot;AHH! NOT THE BOWTIE! ANYTHING BUT THE BOWTIE!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T09:30:50-07:00","id":1482257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1231193-geist-kickstarter-discussion-thread?p=1355727#post1355727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of the Regalia and Ceremonies Chapter is my messy baby. Apologies about the messiness, by the way-the entire process was riddled with a lot of things happening, definitely the roughest period I've written in so far.<br /> <br /> On that note, Vera has final say, but after evaluating the changes and tweaking the values based on the final product, here's what my take on it was*:<br /> <br /> Furies<br /> Bloody Mary Done Me Wrong: 1-Dot<br /> Boulevard of Winters Lost: 3-Dot<br /> Law Writ in Blood: 5-Dot<br /> <br /> Mourners<br /> Play It Forward: 5-Dot<br /> Extended Checkout: 1-Dot<br /> DJ Amadeus's Sick Flow: 3-Dot<br /> <br /> Necropolitans<br /> Come As You Are: 4-Dot<br /> L'amour du Vide: 2-Dot<br /> My Twenty Dollar Cherubim: 3-Dot<br /> <br /> Pilgrims<br /> Losing the Religion: 1-Dot<br /> Tripitaka's Journey: 3-Dot<br /> Running with Atropos' Scissors: 5-Dot<br /> <br /> Undertakers<br /> For Those Who Are Left: 1-Dot<br /> What's Old is New: 2-Dot<br /> Walking the Destroyer's Path: 4-Dot<br /> <br /> *Now mind you, that's with me being a little shaky on the nature of temporary anchors and how to balance that against how some ceremonies are more regular practice and others are grand rituals and honestly that I just basically went wild on the ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have a question about Ceremonies...what is like the idea/system for what constitutes a level 1 or a level 3 ceremony. Because for example the Bloody Codex seems significantly less potent than like Crow Girl Kiss or Lover's Telephone. So, I am clearly missing the idea for what should be what in the terms of levels here.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh shit I didn't see how old this thread was! Sorry for the necrothreading there, but yeah I asked cuz I liked a lot of the ceremonies in Memento Mori","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8100,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","user":"Caedus","date":". 05-29-2022, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}